            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-i" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier type="set" value="1" field="da-wing-hq-damocles-min">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-i" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Stormwing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-0">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-0-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Stormwing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-0-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>First Fire/Overwatch: re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 with Bolters, Bolt Pistols, Storm Bolters, Foeblaster Boltguns and bolter component of combi-weapons. If The Storm of War is selected: stationary Stormwing units also use the Stormwing re-roll during the normal Shooting phase; Stormwing Infantry containing a Stormwing Character gains Stubborn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Deathwing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-1">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-1-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Deathwing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-1-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>With a sword-type weapon against an enemy whose Weapon Skill is higher than the model’s own, re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 in close combat. If The Unbroken Vow is selected: a Deathwing unit within 6" of an Objective gains Feel No Pain (6+), or improves existing Feel No Pain by one step to a maximum of 4+; a Deathwing Independent Character within 12" of an Objective gains +1 Attack.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Dreadwing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-2">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-2-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Dreadwing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-2-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Flame, Plasma and Volkite attacks against this unit are -1 Strength (minimum 1); against Dreadwing Vehicles/Dreadnoughts this also reduces Armour Penetration Strength. If The Eskaton Imperative is selected: Dreadwing Infantry gain Move Through Cover and all Dreadwing models may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Ironwing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-3">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-3-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Ironwing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-3-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Re-roll Armour Penetration rolls of 1 against enemy Vehicles. Ironwing Vehicles firing Snap Shots hit on 5+ instead of 6+. If The Steel Fist is selected: a Transport Vehicle carrying an Ironwing Independent Character gains a 6+ Invulnerable Save against shooting, or improves an existing Invulnerable Save by one step to a maximum of 4+.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Firewing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-4">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-4-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Firewing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-4-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when attacking an enemy unit containing an Independent Character, in shooting and close combat. If The Serpent’s Bane is selected: against a nominated Priority Target, Firewing models re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 and To Wound rolls of 1 (Armour Penetration rolls of 1 against Vehicles); a Firewing Independent Character gains +1 Attack in melee with a Priority Target. Up to three Firewing Troops units may select Forward Deployment — Infiltrate.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Ravenwing" hidden="false" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-5">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="da-wing-hq-damocles-5-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Ravenwing" id="da-wing-hq-damocles-5-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Dark Angels Bikes and Jetbikes gain Skilled Rider; Dark Angels Land Speeders gain Jink. If The Seeker’s Arrow is selected: Ravenwing Infantry, Bikes and Jetbikes gain Outflank; Ravenwing Bikes and Jetbikes gain Hit &amp; Run. At the start of each Dark Angels turn choose +2" Turbo-Boost/Advance, +2" Charge, or +2" Consolidation for all Ravenwing units until the next Dark Angels turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup id="r49-legion-upgrades-hq-damocles" name="Legion Wargear &amp; Upgrades" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
          <entryLinks>
            </entryLinks>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <entryLinks />
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Army Configuration" id="config-army" hidden="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="config-army-min" type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" automatic="true" />
        <constraint id="config-army-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="cat-config" id="config-army-cat" primary="true" name="Configuration" hidden="false" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Choose a Legion" id="config-army-rule" hidden="false">
          <description>Every Legiones Astartes Detachment must belong to exactly one Legion and must declare an Allegiance. The chosen Legion applies its named Legiones Astartes rule to eligible models in the Detachment. Legion-specific units, wargear, characters and Rites of War are only available where their own entries permit them.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r34-supplement-banner" name="Supplementary Units — Opponent Agreement" hidden="false">
          <description>Lords of War and Aeronautica are supplementary choices. Before the battle, agree with your opponent whether these units are permitted and whether your mission, event, or agreed game size imposes any additional restrictions.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Legion" id="config-legion" hidden="false">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="config-legion-min" type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" />
            <constraint id="config-legion-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="I Legion — Dark Angels" id="legion-i" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-i-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Dark Angels)" id="legion-i-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Dark Angels. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Dark Angels). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Mastery of the Blade" id="da22-mastery" hidden="false">
                  <description>When a Dark Angels model fights in close combat using a sword-type weapon against an enemy model with equal Weapon Skill, it hits on a 3+ instead of 4+. Sword-type weapons include Chainswords, Power Weapons, Force Weapons, Rending Weapons and Dark Angels weapons stated to count as swords; not Power Fists, Thunder Hammers, Lightning Claws or other clearly non-sword weapons.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="The Hexagrammaton" id="da22-hexagrammaton" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every Dark Angels unit must be assigned to one Wing: Stormwing, Deathwing, Dreadwing, Ironwing, Firewing or Ravenwing. A unit normally belongs to only one. A Dedicated Transport has the same Wing as the unit that purchased it. Fixed-Wing units and named characters may not choose another Wing. Independent Characters retain their own Wing and do not confer it.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Dark Angels Armoury" id="da22-armoury-summary" hidden="false">
                  <description>Dark Angels gain access to the Legion-specific armoury where the relevant base weapon or Armoury access permits it: Calibanite Warblades, Terranic Greatswords, Ancient Plasma Weaponry, Plasma Repeaters, Plasma Burners, Stasis Shells, Molecular Acid Shells and Teleportation Transponders. Eligibility and prices are represented on the relevant options where implemented.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="III Legion — Emperor's Children" id="legion-iii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-iii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Emperor's Children)" id="legion-iii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Emperor's Children. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Emperor's Children). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Emperor'S Children — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-iii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
EXEMPLARS OF WAR
The Emperor's Children seek perfection in every aspect of warfare, placing particular emphasis upon speed, precision and the flawless execution of carefully prepared battle plans.
Emperor's Children units gain the Crusader special rule.
In addition, during an Assault phase in which an Emperor's Children model charges, that model gains +1 Initiative until the end of that Assault phase. This bonus may be combined with other Initiative modifiers.
PURITY ABOVE ALL
The Emperor's Children place extraordinary importance upon the physical purity and perfection of their warriors, and their Apothecaries hold positions of particular importance within the Legion.
Any Legion Veteran Squad may upgrade its Legion Veteran Sergeant to an Apothecary for +25 points.
In addition, up to one Legion Tactical Squad or Legion Assault Squad in the army may upgrade its Legion Sergeant to an Apothecary for +25 points. The Apothecary retains all weapons and wargear previously carried by the Sergeant and is additionally equipped with a Narthecium.
The Apothecary counts as an Apothecary for all rules and wargear restrictions and may purchase a Reductor for +5 points.
MARTIAL PRIDE
The warriors of the Emperor's Children possess an almost pathological desire to prove their superiority in battle. Retreat from an opponent once battle has been joined is regarded as an admission of inferiority few of Fulgrim's sons are willing to accept.
Emperor's Children units may not voluntarily withdraw from close combat.
In addition, if an Emperor's Children unit wins a close combat and all enemy units it was engaged with retreat, the Emperor's Children unit must Pursue if it is able to do so. It may not take a Restraint Test in order to Consolidate instead.
EMPEROR'S CHILDREN ARMOURY
The III Legion has always placed exceptional value upon weapons of perfect balance, craftsmanship and aesthetic refinement.
As the Horus Heresy progressed, the Traitor elements of the Legion supplemented these masterpieces with increasingly experimental and horrific sonic devices.
PHOENIX SPEAR
An Emperor's Children Independent Character or unit Character able to select a Power Weapon may instead select a Phoenix Spear for +20 points. A model already equipped with a Power Weapon as part of its basic wargear may exchange it for a Phoenix Spear for +5 points.
PHOENIX SPEAR — 20 POINTS
Any Emperor's Children Independent Character or unit Character able to select a Power Weapon may instead select a Phoenix Spear for +20 points. A model already equipped with a Power Weapon as part of its basic wargear may exchange it for a Phoenix Spear for +5 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Phoenix Spear | User | Power Weapon, Two-Handed, Phoenix Strike
Phoenix Strike: During the first round of each close combat, attacks made with a Phoenix Spear are resolved at +1 Strength. After the first round, the weapon is resolved at the bearer's normal Strength.
DIGITAL LASERS
An Emperor's Children Independent Character may purchase Digital Lasers for +15 points. A model equipped with Digital Lasers adds +1 to its Attacks characteristic. Digital Lasers may not be combined with Terminator Honours.
SONIC SHRIEKER
TRAITOR ONLY
Sonic Shriekers are surgically implanted resonators capable of emitting disorientating waves of sound that overwhelm the senses of nearby enemies. An Emperor's Children Independent Character may purchase a Sonic Shrieker for +10 points. Additional units may gain access to Sonic Shriekers through their unit entry or a Rite of War.
During the first round of a close combat, an enemy model in base contact with a model equipped with a Sonic Shrieker suffers -1 Weapon Skill.
If every model in an Emperor's Children unit is equipped with a Sonic Shrieker, every enemy model engaged with that unit suffers -1 Weapon Skill during the first round of close combat instead.
This modifier is not cumulative. Fearless models are unaffected.
SONIC WEAPONRY
TRAITOR ONLY
Certain formations of the Traitor Emperor's Children have begun employing experimental sonic weapons developed from the terrible discoveries made during the Legion's descent into corruption.
One Legion Heavy Support Squad in an Emperor's Children Detachment may select up to four Sonic Weapons instead of selecting weapons from its normal Heavy Weapon options.
Pay the following points cost for each weapon selected:
• Sonic Blaster ........................................ +15 points
• Doom Siren ............................................ +20 points
• Blastmaster ........................................... +35 points
In addition, one Emperor's Children Praetor or Centurion in the army may select one of the following:
• Sonic Blaster ........................................ +15 points
• Doom Siren ............................................ +20 points
A Character may carry no more than one Sonic Weapon.
SONIC WEAPONS — TRAITOR ONLY
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Type
Sonic Blaster | 24" | 4 | 5 | Assault 2 or Heavy 3
Doom Siren | Template | 5 | 4 | Assault 1
Blastmaster | 48" | 8 | 3 | Heavy 1, Blast
PERFECT CACOPHONY
A Legion Heavy Support Squad in which the majority of surviving models are equipped with Sonic Weapons may purchase the Fearless special rule for +20 points per squad.
EMPEROR'S CHILDREN RITE OF WAR:
THE MARU SKARA
The Maru Skara is one of the most celebrated battle doctrines of the Emperor's Children: a carefully orchestrated feint in which the visible strength of the Legion fixes the enemy in place while a concealed blade manoeuvres to deliver the killing stroke.
EFFECTS
THE OPEN BLADE
All units deployed normally at the beginning of the battle form the Open Blade.
The army's Warlord must form part of the Open Blade and must begin the battle on the battlefield.
THE HIDDEN BLADE
Before deployment, nominate up to three Emperor's Children units selected from the following:
• Legion Assault Squads
• Legion Veteran Squads
• Legion Terminator Squads
• Palatine Blade Squads
• Phoenix Terminator Squads
• Legion Bike Squadrons
• Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons
An Independent Character may accompany a nominated unit normally.
Dedicated Transports purchased for a nominated unit form part of the Hidden Blade with that unit.
All units forming the Hidden Blade must begin the battle in Reserve.
PERFECTLY TIMED STRIKE
After deployment zones have been determined but before either army deploys, secretly record:
• either game turn 2 or game turn 3;
• either the left or right side table edge.
Do not reveal this choice to the opposing player.
At the beginning of the chosen Emperor's Children turn, reveal the recorded choice.
Every surviving unit of the Hidden Blade becomes available automatically without making a Reserve roll.
These units enter play from the chosen side table edge.
They may act normally during the turn in which they arrive.
THE KILLING STROKE
During the player turn in which the Hidden Blade arrives, all Emperor's Children units may re-roll failed Advance rolls and failed Charge distance rolls. The second result must be accepted.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must begin the battle as part of the Open Blade.
The Hidden Blade may contain no more than three units, excluding attached Independent Characters and Dedicated Transports.
The army may include no more than two Heavy Support choices.
Immobile units may not be selected.
EMPEROR'S CHILDREN RITE OF WAR:
3RD COMPANY ELITE
TRAITOR ONLY
As the III Legion descended into corruption, entire formations embraced the experimental sonic augmentations first developed amongst the Kakophoni. The most infamous of these formations was the 3rd Company, whose warriors willingly submitted themselves to increasingly extreme surgical and sonic modification.
EFFECTS
CHOSEN OF VAIROSEAN
Kakophoni Squads may be selected as Troops choices. Kakophoni Squads selected as Troops may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
All Kakophoni Squads in the Detachment gain the Relentless special rule.
SONIC ASSAULT
Any Emperor's Children Infantry unit composed entirely of models wearing Power Armour or Artificer Armour may purchase Sonic Shriekers for +2 points per model. Every eligible model in the unit must purchase the upgrade.
A unit equipped in this manner follows the normal Sonic Shrieker rules.
ARMOURY OF EXCESS
The normal restriction allowing only one Legion Heavy Support Squad to select Sonic Weaponry is removed.
Up to two Legion Heavy Support Squads may select Sonic Weaponry when using this Rite of War.
PERFECT CACOPHONY
A unit in which every surviving model is equipped with either a Sonic Weapon or Sonic Shrieker gains the Fear special rule.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Traitor Emperor's Children Detachment.
The army must include at least one Kakophoni Squad.
The army's Warlord must either:
• be equipped with a Sonic Shrieker; or
• be a named Character whose rules specifically associate him with the Kakophoni or 3rd Company.
The army may include no more than one Fortification.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r52-ec-exemplars" name="Exemplars of War" hidden="false">
                  <description>Emperor's Children units gain Crusader. During an Assault phase in which an Emperor's Children model charges, it gains +1 Initiative until the end of that Assault phase; this may combine with other Initiative modifiers.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r52-ec-purity" name="Purity Above All" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any Legion Veteran Squad may upgrade its Legion Veteran Sergeant to an Apothecary for +25 points. In addition, up to one Legion Tactical Squad or Legion Assault Squad may upgrade its Legion Sergeant to an Apothecary for +25 points. The Apothecary gains a Narthecium and may purchase a Reductor for +5 points.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r52-ec-martial" name="Martial Pride" hidden="false">
                  <description>Emperor's Children units may not voluntarily withdraw from close combat. If they win a close combat and all engaged enemy units retreat, they must Pursue if able and may not take a Restraint Test to Consolidate instead.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="IV Legion — Iron Warriors" id="legion-iv" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-iv-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors)" id="legion-iv-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Iron Warriors. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Iron Warriors — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-iv-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
SIEGE MASTERS
The Iron Warriors are the foremost practitioners of siege warfare amongst the Legiones Astartes, trained to identify structural weaknesses, endure prolonged bombardment and reduce even the strongest fortifications through methodical application of force.
Non-vehicle models with the Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors) special rule receive +1 to Armour Penetration rolls made against Fortifications, Buildings, Bunkers, Tank Traps and other immobile structures with an Armour Value.
In addition, Iron Warriors models only trigger enemy Minefields on a roll of 6.
An Iron Warriors unit occupying a friendly Fortification or Bunker gains the Stubborn special rule.
This rule provides no benefit while occupying a Fortification belonging to the enemy at the beginning of the battle.
AN ARMY OF STEEL AND WRATH
The Iron Warriors favour overwhelming concentrations of artillery, heavy armour and siege engines, accepting a corresponding reduction in the number of rapid assault formations deployed alongside them.
When constructing an Iron Warriors Detachment, the player may exchange two Fast Attack selections for one additional Heavy Support selection.
This exchange may only be made once.
When using the Standard Force Organisation Chart, an Iron Warriors army may therefore include:
• 0–1 Fast Attack choices
• 0–4 Heavy Support choices
All other Force Organisation limits remain unchanged.
STUBBORN RESOLVE
The Iron Warriors possess a grim refusal to accept defeat, often continuing an engagement long after another commander would have ordered a withdrawal.
If a mission uses a variable game length and the game would normally end, the opposing player may demand that one additional complete game turn be played. Roll a D6. On a roll of 3+, one additional complete game turn is played.
This roll may only be made once. After the additional game turn has been completed, the battle ends automatically.
This rule has no effect in a mission which ends immediately when a particular objective or action is completed once that objective or action has already occurred.
PRELIMINARY BOMBARDMENT
The Iron Warriors routinely precede major assaults with prolonged and precisely coordinated artillery bombardments.
This rule only applies in missions which already use Preliminary Bombardment.
When resolving a Preliminary Bombardment, the Iron Warriors player receives one additional Preliminary Bombardment roll for every full 500 points in the army.
Before any Preliminary Bombardment rolls are made, each additional roll must be assigned to an eligible enemy unit or obstacle.
Several additional rolls may be assigned to the same target, but all rolls assigned to that target must be made together.
Additional rolls may not be assigned after bombardment rolls have begun.
Resolve these additional attacks using the normal Preliminary Bombardment rules.
IRON WARRIORS ARMOURY
The IV Legion has little interest in ornament or ritual craftsmanship. Its arsenals favour weapons and equipment designed for prolonged siege warfare, suppression and the methodical destruction of fortified positions.
SHRAPNEL BOLTS — 5 POINTS PER UNIT
The following weapons carried by models in the unit gain the Pinning special rule: Bolt Pistols, Bolters, Combi-Bolters, Storm Bolters, Heavy Bolters, Twin-linked Bolters and the bolter component of Combi-Weapons.Shrapnel Bolts may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition, Hellfire Rounds or another special ammunition type.
SERVO-ARM
Any Iron Warriors model with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Servo-Arm for +30 points, even if the model is not normally permitted to select Techmarine equipment.
The Servo-Arm follows the normal rules presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List.
A model equipped with a Jump Pack may not purchase a Servo-Arm.
BIONICS
Iron Warriors have long made extensive use of extensive cybernetic reconstruction to return wounded Legionaries to battle.
Any Iron Warriors model with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase Bionics for +5 points instead of the normal +10 points.
Bionics otherwise follow the normal rules presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List.
IRON WARRIORS RITE OF WAR:
THE HAMMER OF OLYMPIA
The Hammer of Olympia represents the characteristic method of war favoured by Perturabo's Grand Battalions: massed infantry advancing beneath disciplined fire while armoured formations grind inexorably forward alongside them.
EFFECTS
THE IRON LINE
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be selected from:
• Legion Tactical Squads
• Legion Breacher Siege Squads
Compulsory Troops choices gain Shrapnel Bolts at no additional points cost.
HAIL OF FIRE
Iron Warriors Tactical Squads and Breacher Siege Squads equipped with Shrapnel Bolts may declare a charge after firing Rapid Fire weapons during the Shooting phase. A unit which does so does not receive the normal +1 Attack bonus for charging during that Assault phase.
A unit which used Fury of the Legion during the same player turn may not benefit from this rule.
FURY OF OLYMPIA
Models equipped with Shrapnel Bolts may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when firing those weapons at an enemy unit within 12".
This benefit does not apply when firing Snap Shots.
ARMOURED RESOLVE
The following Iron Warriors vehicles ignore Crew Shaken and Crew Stunned results:
• Legion Predator Strike Squadrons
• Legion Vindicator Siege Tank Squadrons
• Land Raiders
• Legion Spartan Assault Tanks
Other results on the Vehicle Damage table apply normally.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must possess the Master of the Legion special rule.
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Legion Tactical Squads or Legion Breacher Siege Squads.
No Iron Warriors unit may deploy using Deep Strike.
Units which are required to enter play by Deep Strike may not be selected.
IRON WARRIORS RITE OF WAR:
THE IRONFIRE
The Ironfire is a siege doctrine in which artillery fire is advanced across the battlefield immediately ahead of the Legion's assault formations.
Iron Warriors infantry advance through explosions, collapsing structures and clouds of debris, trusting their gunners to place each successive salvo only metres ahead of their position.
EFFECTS
ARTILLERY COLUMN
One Legion Artillery Tank Squadron may be selected as a non-compulsory Troops choice.
An Artillery Tank Squadron selected in this manner:
• does not occupy a Heavy Support choice;
• may not fulfil a compulsory Troops selection;
• does not count as a Scoring Unit unless it would normally do so for another reason.
The normal 0–1 restriction on Legion Artillery Tank Squadrons still applies.
ROLLING BOMBARDMENT
When an Iron Warriors Barrage weapon fires at a point within 12" of a friendly Iron Warriors unit, reduce its scatter distance.
If the attack would normally scatter 2D6", it scatters only D6" instead.
After resolving the Barrage attack, place an Ironfire Marker at the final centre point of the Blast marker.
WALKING THE FIRE
When another Iron Warriors Barrage weapon fires, it does not scatter if the initial target point is:
• within 18" of an Ironfire Marker; AND
• within 6" of a friendly Iron Warriors unit.
After resolving the attack, place a new Ironfire Marker at the centre of the Blast marker as normal.
If an Iron Warriors Shooting phase ends without a new Ironfire Marker being placed, remove all Ironfire Markers from the battlefield.
RIDE THE IRONFIRE
Iron Warriors Infantry units with at least one model within 6" of an Ironfire Marker gain the Fearless special rule.
This benefit lasts only while at least one model in the unit remains within 6" of an Ironfire Marker.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must possess the Master of the Legion special rule.
The army must contain at least one unit equipped with a Barrage weapon.
If the mission designates one player as the Attacker and the other as the Defender, the Iron Warriors must be the Attacker.
The army may not include a Fortification.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r57-iw-siege" name="Siege Masters" hidden="false">
                  <description>Non-vehicle Iron Warriors receive +1 Armour Penetration against Fortifications, Buildings, Bunkers, Tank Traps and other immobile AV structures. Iron Warriors trigger enemy Minefields only on a 6. An Iron Warriors unit in a friendly Fortification or Bunker gains Stubborn; no benefit in an enemy-starting Fortification.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r57-iw-steel" name="An Army of Steel and Wrath" hidden="false">
                  <description>Once per detachment, exchange two Fast Attack selections for one additional Heavy Support selection. On the standard chart this gives 0–1 Fast Attack and 0–4 Heavy Support.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r57-iw-stubborn" name="Stubborn Resolve" hidden="false">
                  <description>If a mission uses variable game length and would end, the opposing player may demand one additional complete game turn; on a 3+ play it. This roll is made only once and the battle ends automatically after that extra turn. No effect after a mission-ending objective/action has already occurred.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r57-iw-prelim" name="Preliminary Bombardment" hidden="false">
                  <description>Only in missions already using Preliminary Bombardment: gain one additional bombardment roll per full 500 points in the army. Assign all additional rolls before any are made; multiple may target the same eligible target and are rolled together.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="V Legion — White Scars" id="legion-v" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-v-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (White Scars)" id="legion-v-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is White Scars. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (White Scars). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="White Scars — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-v-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
SWIFT ADVANCE
The warriors of the White Scars place speed and freedom of movement above rigid battle lines, advancing rapidly across the battlefield before the enemy can react.
A White Scars Infantry unit composed entirely of models wearing Power Armour, Artificer Armour or Recon Armour may make a Swift Advance.
During its Shooting phase, the unit may forgo shooting and instead move an additional D6".
A unit making a Swift Advance:
• may move even if it made a Normal Move during the preceding Movement phase;
• is not slowed by Difficult Terrain during this additional movement;
• may not move within 1" of an enemy model;
• may not charge during the same player turn.
Models wearing any form of Terminator Armour or Hardened Armour may not use Swift Advance.
BORN IN THE SADDLE
The warriors of the V Legion are without equal in mounted warfare, controlling their Bikes and Jetbikes as naturally as another warrior might wield a blade.
White Scars models mounted on Bikes or Jetbikes gain the Skilled Rider special rule.
In addition, the following units gain the Hit &amp; Run special rule:
• Legion Bike Squadrons
• Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons
The unit may only use Hit &amp; Run if every model in the unit, including any attached Independent Character, is mounted on a Bike or Jetbike.
Legion Attack Bike Squadrons do not gain Hit &amp; Run from this rule.
MOUNTED BROTHERHOODS
Many White Scars Brotherhoods wage entire campaigns from the saddle, their massed Bike formations forming the main battle line rather than merely supporting it.
Legion Bike Squadrons may be selected as Troops choices in a White Scars Detachment.
Legion Bike Squadrons selected as Troops may fulfil the army's compulsory Troops selections.
They are otherwise identical to the Legion Bike Squadron entry in the Legiones Astartes Army List.
WHITE SCARS ARMOURY
The warriors of the V Legion carry weapons and tokens whose origins lie in the ancient traditions of Chogoris, adapted to the needs of the Great Crusade without losing their ritual significance.
POWER GLAIVE — 25 POINTS
Any White Scars Character able to select a Power Weapon may instead select a Power Glaive for +25 points. A model already equipped with a Power Weapon as part of its basic wargear may exchange it for a Power Glaive for +10 points.
At the beginning of each Assault phase, the bearer must choose how the Power Glaive is wielded. The chosen mode is used for the remainder of that Assault phase.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Power Glaive — One-Handed | User | Power Weapon
Power Glaive — Two-Handed | User +1 | Power Weapon, Two-Handed
CHOGORIAN WARLANCE — 15 POINTS
Any White Scars model with access to the Space Marine Armoury that is mounted on a Bike or Jetbike may purchase a Chogorian Warlance for +15 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Chogorian Warlance | User | Power Weapon, Cavalry Lance
Cavalry Lance: During the first round of a close combat in which the bearer charged, the bearer receives +1 Initiative. During any round of close combat in which the bearer did not charge, the bearer instead suffers -1 Initiative. A Chogorian Warlance is a one-handed weapon.
CYBER-HAWK
One White Scars Praetor may purchase a Cyber-hawk for +10 points.
At the beginning of each White Scars turn, place the Cyber-hawk marker anywhere on the battlefield.
The marker may be moved to a different position at the beginning of each subsequent White Scars turn.
When a White Scars Infantry unit attacks an enemy unit with at least one model within 6" of the Cyber-hawk:
• it may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when making shooting attacks;
• its charge distance against that enemy unit is increased from 6" to 7".
The Cyber-hawk is only a marker. It cannot be attacked, does not block movement or line of sight and has no characteristics of its own.
HORSETAIL TALISMAN
One White Scars Independent Character may purchase a Horsetail Talisman for +25 points.
Only one Horsetail Talisman may be included in an army.
Once per battle, at the beginning of the White Scars Shooting phase, the bearer may reveal the Horsetail Talisman.
The bearer and every friendly White Scars non-vehicle unit with at least one model within 6" may choose to move D6" instead of shooting.
Bike and Jetbike units may also make this movement.
A unit which makes this move:
• may not move within 1" of an enemy model;
• must maintain unit coherency;
• may not charge during the same player turn.
Units which are Falling Back, embarked upon a Transport or locked in close combat may not benefit.
STORMSEER CONSUL — +35 POINTS
A White Scars Legion Centurion may be upgraded to a Stormseer Consul for +35 points. A White Scars army may not select the normal Legion Librarian Consul upgrade. It uses the Stormseer Consul instead.
Wargear:
• Replace the Centurion's Chainsword with a Force Weapon
Special Rules:
• Psyker (Mastery Level 1\)
• Adamantium Will
• Legion Support Officer
PSYCHIC POWERS
A Stormseer knows the Unseen Bolt psychic power.
Unseen Bolt | 36" | 6 | 4 | Assault 1, Blast, Pinning
UNSEEN BOLT
Unseen Bolt is a psychic shooting power. It is used during the Stormseer's Shooting phase instead of firing another weapon.
Take a Psychic test using the normal ProHammer psychic rules. If successful, resolve the attack using the profile above. Unseen Bolt may not be invoked during Return Fire, Overwatch or Stand &amp; Shoot.
Epistolary
A Stormseer may be upgraded to Mastery Level 2 for a further +25 points.
If upgraded to Mastery Level 2, he may select one additional psychic power from the normal Legion Librarian Psychic Powers list.
OPTIONS
• A Stormseer may purchase:
• Psychic Hood .................................. +25 points
All other equipment is selected normally from the Space Marine Armoury.
WHITE SCARS RITE OF WAR:
CHOGORIAN BROTHERHOOD
The Chogorian Brotherhood is the archetypal war formation of the V Legion: a rapidly moving host of mounted warriors supported by mobile infantry and reconnaissance elements, striking from unexpected directions before disappearing beyond retaliation.
EFFECTS
RIDE LIKE THE WIND
Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons may be selected as Troops choices.
Legion Bike Squadrons and Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
LIGHTNING ENCIRCLEMENT
The following White Scars units gain the Outflank special rule:
• Legion Bike Squadrons
• Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons
• Legion Attack Bike Squadrons
• Legion Land Speeder Squadrons
• Javelin Attack Speeder Squadrons
In addition, White Scars Infantry units gain Outflank provided that the unit contains no model wearing Terminator Armour or carrying a Heavy weapon. A Dedicated Transport purchased for a unit deploying by Outflank may enter play with that unit.
MASTER OF THE HUNT
The White Scars player may re-roll Reserve rolls for units in this Detachment. The player may choose to re-roll either a successful or failed Reserve roll. The second result must be accepted.
STRIKE AND VANISH
A White Scars Bike or Jetbike unit which successfully uses Hit &amp; Run may roll one additional D6 for its Hit &amp; Run movement and discard the lowest result.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be mounted on either:
• a Space Marine Bike; or
• a Jetbike.
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Legion Bike Squadrons or Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons.
The army may include no more than one Heavy Support choice. If every Bike and Jetbike unit in the Detachment has been completely destroyed by the end of the battle, the enemy receives an additional 150 Victory Points. This penalty only applies in missions using Victory Points.
WHITE SCARS RITE OF WAR:
THE SAGYAR MAZAN
LOYALIST ONLY
The Sagyar Mazan are warriors condemned by dishonour, disobedience or catastrophic failure. Rather than face execution at the hands of their brothers, these penitents are permitted to seek absolution through death in battle.
They do not fight for survival. They fight so that their deaths may have meaning.
EFFECTS
DEATH SEEKERS
Whenever a non-vehicle White Scars unit from this Detachment is completely destroyed and would award Victory Points to the enemy, roll a D6.
1–3: Resolve Victory Points normally.
4–5: The destroyed unit awards no Victory Points.
6: The destroyed unit awards no Victory Points and the White Scars player instead gains 50 Victory Points.
This roll is made separately for each destroyed unit.
THE SERPENT'S EYE
During the first round of any close combat, non-vehicle White Scars units from this Detachment gain the Fearless special rule. This applies whether the unit charged or was charged.
NOT YET DEAD
Non-vehicle White Scars units gain Feel No Pain (6+). If a unit already possesses Feel No Pain, improve its Feel No Pain roll by one step, to a maximum of 4+.
EBON KESHIG
Ebon Keshig units may be selected as Troops choices. They may fulfil compulsory Troops selections. This rule has no effect until the Ebon Keshig army list entry is used.
LIMITATIONS
SEEK DEATH, DO NOT HIDE FROM IT
No unit in the Detachment may voluntarily begin the battle in Reserve. Units which are required by their own rules to begin in Reserve may not be selected.
NO PATH OF RETREAT
Units in this Detachment may not voluntarily withdraw from close combat. If they win a close combat and the enemy retreats, they must Pursue whenever they are able to do so.
THE PENITENT HOST
This Rite may only be used by a Loyalist White Scars Detachment. The Detachment may not include Jaghatai Khan.The army may not include a Fortification. The army may never contain more Vehicle units than non-vehicle Infantry units.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r60-ws-swift" name="Swift Advance" hidden="false">
                  <description>Eligible White Scars Infantry in Power, Artificer or Recon Armour may forgo shooting to move an additional D6 inches. This move ignores Difficult Terrain, may not move within 1 inch of the enemy and the unit may not charge that turn. Terminator and Hardened Armour may not use this rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r60-ws-saddle" name="Born in the Saddle" hidden="false">
                  <description>White Scars models on Bikes or Jetbikes gain Skilled Rider. Legion Bike and Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons also gain Hit &amp; Run while every model in the unit, including attached Independent Characters, is mounted on a Bike or Jetbike. Attack Bikes do not gain Hit &amp; Run from this rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r60-ws-mounted" name="Mounted Brotherhoods" hidden="false">
                  <description>Legion Bike Squadrons may be selected as Troops and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="VI Legion — Space Wolves" id="legion-vi" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-vi-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)" id="legion-vi-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Space Wolves. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Space Wolves — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-vi-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
HUNTERS OF FENRIS
The warriors of the VI Legion possess instincts honed by the death world of Fenris and a natural talent for meeting an enemy assault with overwhelming violence.
All non-vehicle units with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule gain the Counter-Attack and Acute Senses special rules.
NO MATTER THE ODDS
Space Wolves refuse to measure victory by numbers and will fight on regardless of how badly the battle turns against them.
Space Wolves units ignore negative Leadership modifiers applied to Break Tests caused by losing close combat.
Other Leadership modifiers apply normally.
BLOOD FEUD
The Space Wolves maintain ancient and bitter rivalries with certain brother Legions.
Space Wolves models always hit Dark Angels and Thousand Sons models on a 3+ in close combat unless they would normally hit on a better result. Dark Angels and Thousand Sons models likewise always hit Space Wolves models on a 3+ in close combat unless they would normally hit on a better result.
LEGION ORGANISATION
The VI Legion is divided into fiercely independent Great Companies, each led by its own Jarl and supported by trusted champions and priests.
A Space Wolves Detachment must include one HQ selection for every full or partial 750 points in the army:
Up to 750 points: 1 HQ
751–1,500 points: 2 HQ
1,501–2,250 points: 3 HQ
2,251–3,000 points: 4 HQ
This replaces the normal minimum and maximum number of HQ selections. The normal restriction on models with Master of the Legion still applies. Space Wolves may not select Legion Chaplain Consuls or Legion Librarian Consuls. Their roles are instead fulfilled by Wolf Priests and Rune Priests.
SPACE WOLVES ARMOURY
The warriors of the VI Legion carry weapons and talismans rooted in the traditions of Fenris. To outsiders many of these objects appear primitive or superstitious, yet their effectiveness in the hands of the Rout is beyond dispute.
FROST WEAPON — 20 POINTS
Any Space Wolves Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Frost Weapon for +20 points. A model already equipped with a Power Weapon may exchange it for a Frost Weapon for +5 points.
A Frost Weapon may be represented by a sword, axe, claw or similar Fenrisian weapon. Its exact appearance has no additional rules effect.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Frost Weapon | User +1 | Power Weapon
GREAT FROST BLADE — 35 POINTS
A Space Wolves Independent Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Great Frost Blade for +35 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Great Frost Blade | User +2 | Power Weapon, Two-Handed, Master-crafted
A model using a Great Frost Blade suffers -1 Initiative during that Assault phase.
WOLF PELT — 5 POINTS
Any Space Wolves Character may purchase a Wolf Pelt for +5 points.
When the bearer's unit successfully uses the Counter-Attack special rule, the bearer receives +2 Attacks instead of the normal +1 Attack granted by Counter-Attack. This bonus applies only to the bearer.
WOLF TOOTH NECKLACE — 10 POINTS
Any Space Wolves Character may purchase a Wolf Tooth Necklace for +10 points.
The bearer always hits enemy models on a 3+ in close combat, regardless of comparative Weapon Skill.
This rule has no effect if the bearer would normally hit on a better result.
WOLF TAIL TALISMAN — 5 POINTS
Any Space Wolves Character may purchase a Wolf Tail Talisman for +5 points.
Whenever an enemy psychic power directly affects the bearer or a unit he has joined, roll a D6 after the power has been successfully invoked and any normal attempt to Deny the Witch has been resolved. On a roll of 6, the bearer is unaffected by that psychic power.
If the bearer is part of a unit, the power affects the remainder of the unit normally.
RUNIC ARMOUR — 25 POINTS
A Space Wolves Independent Character wearing Power Armour may replace it with Runic Armour for +25 points. Runic Armour grants:
• a 2+ Armour Save;
• the Adamantium Will special rule.
Runic Armour counts as Artificer Armour for all other rules and restrictions. A model wearing Runic Armour may carry a Wolf Tail Talisman normally.
WOLF PRIEST CONSUL — +35 POINTS
A Legion Centurion with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule may be upgraded to a Wolf Priest for +35 points. A Space Wolves army may not select a Legion Chaplain Consul.
Wargear:
• Replace the Wolf Priest's Chainsword with a Fang of Morkai.
• Rosarius.
Special Rules:
• Rites of Battle
• Oath of the Slayer
FANG OF MORKAI
The Fang of Morkai counts as a Power Weapon.
RITES OF BATTLE
The Wolf Priest and any Space Wolves unit he has joined may re-roll failed Morale checks.
OATH OF THE SLAYER
Before deployment, nominate one enemy unit. The Wolf Priest and any Space Wolves unit he has joined may re-roll failed To Hit rolls in close combat against the nominated enemy unit. The oath lasts for the duration of the battle.
RUNE PRIEST CONSUL — +25 POINTS
A Legion Centurion with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule may be upgraded to a Rune Priest for +25 points. A Space Wolves army may not select a Legion Librarian Consul.
Wargear:
• Replace the Rune Priest's Chainsword with a Runic Force Weapon.
• Wolf Tail Talisman.
Special Rules:
• Psyker (Mastery Level 1\)
• Legion Support Officer
Psychic Powers:
• Mystic Winds of Fenris
OPTIONS
• The Rune Priest may be upgraded to a Master of Runes
for +25 points.
A Master of Runes has Psychic Mastery Level 2 and may select one additional psychic power from the disciplines normally available to a Legion Librarian.
• The Rune Priest may purchase a Psychic Hood from the
Space Marine Armoury as normal.
RUNIC FORCE WEAPON
A Runic Force Weapon counts as a Force Weapon.
MYSTIC WINDS OF FENRIS
Blessing — Friendly Space Wolves unit within 6". If the Psychic Test is passed, nominate the Rune Priest or one friendly Space Wolves unit with at least one model within 6". Until the beginning of the next Space Wolves turn, the nominated unit receives a 5+ Cover Save. If the unit already has a Cover Save, improve that save by 1, to a maximum of 4+.
SPACE WOLVES RITE OF WAR:
THE PALE HUNTERS
The Pale Hunters represent the Rout at its most patient. The prey is encircled, exhausted and driven from safety before the Wolves close from every direction for the kill.
EFFECTS
THE GREAT HUNT
Add +1 to Reserve rolls made for Space Wolves units in this Detachment.
HUNTERS WITHOUT PEER
All non-vehicle Space Wolves units gain the Hit &amp; Run special rule provided that the unit contains no model wearing any form of Terminator Armour. Unlike normal Hit &amp; Run, a unit which gains the rule through The Pale Hunters moves 2D6" after successfully disengaging rather than the normal 3D6".
THE KILLING BLOW
During an Assault phase in which a Space Wolves unit successfully charged, models in that unit gain one additional Attack.
This is in addition to the normal +1 Attack for charging. This bonus does not apply to a unit making a Disordered Charge or to a unit which would otherwise receive no charging bonus.
PACK HUNTERS
When two or more friendly Space Wolves units are engaged with the same enemy unit, each participating Space Wolves unit adds +1 to its combat-resolution score. This bonus is not cumulative regardless of how many Space Wolves units are involved.
LIMITATIONS
The army may include no more than one Heavy Support choice.
The army may not include:
• Legion Artillery Tank Squadrons;
• Rapier Weapons Batteries;
• Drop Pods;
• Dreadnought Drop Pods;
• Dreadclaw Drop Pods.
A model wearing any form of Terminator Armour does not gain Hit &amp; Run from this Rite.
SPACE WOLVES RITE OF WAR:
THE BLOODIED CLAWS
There are battles in which manoeuvre and patience serve no purpose. When Russ orders the enemy line broken, the Rout commits itself to a single overwhelming assault intended to tear the heart from the foe in one act of controlled savagery.
EFFECTS
BREAK THE LINE
Space Wolves units add +1 to their combat-resolution score while at least half of the models in the unit are within the enemy deployment zone.
This bonus is not cumulative with itself.
HOWL OF THE DEATH WOLF
Once per battle, at the beginning of a Space Wolves turn, the Warlord may unleash the Howl of the Death Wolf.
Until the end of that player turn:
• Space Wolves units may re-roll their Advance roll;
• the normal charge distance of Space Wolves units is increased from 6" to 7".
A re-rolled Advance result must be accepted.
UNSTOPPABLE VIOLENCE
During an Assault phase in which a Space Wolves unit charges an enemy unit that is already engaged by another friendly Space Wolves unit, that charging unit gains the Furious Charge special rule for that Assault phase.
BLOODIED CLAWS
Grey Slayer Squads and Legion Assault Squads must declare a charge during the Assault phase if there is an enemy unit within their legal charge distance. If more than one enemy unit is within range, the Space Wolves player may choose which enemy unit is charged.
LIMITATIONS
NO PREY LEFT UNHUNTED
Grey Slayer Squads may fulfil compulsory Troops selections when using this Rite.
At least one compulsory Troops choice must be a Grey Slayer Squad.
NO PATH OF RETREAT
Units in this Detachment may not voluntarily withdraw from close combat.
If a Space Wolves unit wins a close combat and an enemy unit retreats, the Space Wolves must Pursue whenever they are able to do so.
THE BREAKING OF THE LINE
The Detachment may not include:
• Artillery units;
• units with the Slow and Purposeful special rule;
• Immobile units;
• Fortifications.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment belonging to another Space Marine Legion.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="VII Legion — Imperial Fists" id="legion-vii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-vii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists)" id="legion-vii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Imperial Fists. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Imperial Fists — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-vii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULE
DISCIPLINED FIRE
The Imperial Fists are renowned for disciplined marksmanship and the maintenance of carefully prepared fields of fire.
When an Imperial Fists unit makes a First Fire or Overwatch shooting attack, models in the unit may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when firing:
• Bolters
• Bolt Pistols
• Combi-Bolters
• Storm Bolters
• Heavy Bolters
• the bolter component of a Combi-weapon
FORTIFICATION MASTERS
The Imperial Fists possess an unrivalled understanding of defensive warfare and the construction and reduction of fortifications.
Imperial Fists models receive +1 to Armour Penetration rolls against Fortifications, Buildings, Bunkers and other immobile structures with an Armour Value. A non-vehicle Imperial Fists unit occupying a friendly Fortification or Bunker gains the Stubborn special rule.
This rule provides no benefit while occupying an enemy Fortification.
If the Imperial Fists are the defenders in a mission which permits the placement of Fortifications or Obstacles, they may place D3 additional 6" sections of razor wire or tank traps.
These must be placed wholly within the Imperial Fists deployment zone.
BLIND TO THE RISK
Imperial Fists possess an uncompromising determination which can drive them to continue fighting even when withdrawal would be the wiser course.
In a mission with variable game length, when the battle would normally end, the opposing player may demand that one additional complete game turn be played. After this additional game turn has been completed, the battle ends automatically.
This rule has no effect if the mission has already ended because a specific objective or action has been completed.
IMPERIAL FISTS ARMOURY
The VII Legion maintains vast arsenals of siege equipment, relic weapons and defensive technologies accumulated over the long years of the Great Crusade.
The following items may be selected in addition to the normal Space Marine Armoury where permitted.
SOLARITE POWER GAUNTLET — 30 POINTS
Any Imperial Fists Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Solarite Power Gauntlet for +30 points. A model already equipped with a Power Fist may exchange it for a Solarite Power Gauntlet for +5 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Solarite Power Gauntlet | 10 | Power Weapon, Unwieldy, Specialist Weapon
Unlike a normal Power Fist, the Solarite Power Gauntlet always strikes at Strength 10 regardless of the bearer's Strength characteristic.
VIGIL PATTERN STORM SHIELD
An Imperial Fists Independent Character may purchase a Vigil Pattern Storm Shield for +25 points.
The bearer may carry no more than one weapon in addition to the shield.
A Vigil Pattern Storm Shield grants a 3+ Invulnerable Save.
The shield occupies one hand and the bearer may never receive the bonus Attack for fighting with two close-combat weapons.
Other Imperial Fists units may gain access to Vigil Pattern Storm Shields through their individual army list entries.
The Vigil Pattern Storm Shield is unique to the Imperial Fists and does not make Storm Shields generally available to the Legiones Astartes.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Imperial Fists unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit.
An Imperial Fists Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +10 points.
A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit Deep Strike. An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
IMPERIAL FISTS RITE OF WAR:
THE STONE GAUNTLET
The Stone Gauntlet is the embodiment of the VII Legion's doctrine of unyielding defence.
Warriors advance shoulder to shoulder behind interlocking shields, absorbing the fury of the enemy before crushing resistance beneath a methodical counter-assault.
EFFECTS
WARDERS OF THE PHALANX
Phalanx Warder Squads may be selected as Troops choices.
They may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
Legion Breacher Siege Squads may also fulfil compulsory Troops selections normally.
SHIELD WALL
An Imperial Fists Infantry unit in which every model is equipped with either a Boarding Shield or Vigil Pattern Storm Shield may form a Shield Wall. The Shield Wall is active provided that:
• the unit did not Advance during its preceding Movement phase;
• the unit is not Falling Back;
• the unit did not charge during the current player turn.
While the Shield Wall is active, models in the unit may re-roll failed Invulnerable Saves granted by Boarding Shields or Vigil Pattern Storm Shields. A re-rolled save may never be re-rolled again.
UNYIELDING LINE
While its Shield Wall is active, the unit gains the Stubborn special rule and may re-roll failed Pinning tests.
THE HAMMER BEHIND THE SHIELD
Models equipped with Boarding Shields gain the Hammer of Wrath special rule.
This uses the normal ProHammer definition of Hammer of Wrath.
A model does not receive an additional attack; instead, one of its normally allowed attacks may be resolved at Initiative 10 during a turn in which it charges.
LIMITATIONS
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be selected from:
• Legion Breacher Siege Squads
• Phalanx Warder Squads
The Detachment must include at least one Independent Character equipped with either a Boarding Shield or Vigil Pattern Storm Shield.
No unit in the Detachment may voluntarily deploy using Deep Strike.
The army may include no more than one Fast Attack choice.
IMPERIAL FISTS RITE OF WAR:
HAMMERFALL STRIKE FORCE
Originally devised for forces deployed from the Phalanx, the Hammerfall Strike Force concentrates elite ship-borne formations for sudden teleport assaults into the heart of the enemy position.
EFFECTS
LANDING FORCE
Phalanx Warder Squads may be selected as Troops choices.
They may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
TELEPORT ARRAY
Any Imperial Fists Infantry unit may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit.
An Imperial Fists Independent Character may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +10 points.
This overrides the normal restriction limiting Teleportation Transponders to models wearing Terminator Armour.
A unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit Deep Strike.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
BLINDING LUMINESCENCE
An Imperial Fists unit arriving by Deep Strike using Teleportation Transponders gains the Shrouded special rule from the moment it is placed on the battlefield until the beginning of its next player turn.
After the unit has been placed, every enemy unit with at least one model:
• within 12" of the arriving unit; and
• with line of sight to at least one model in the arriving unit
must immediately take an Initiative test. If the test is failed, that enemy unit suffers the effects of the Blind special rule:
• Weapon Skill 1
• Ballistic Skill 1
until the end of its next player turn.
Each enemy unit only makes one such test per arriving Imperial Fists unit.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be equipped with Teleportation Transponders.
Every Vehicle in the Detachment must begin the battle in Reserve.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
IMPERIAL FISTS RITE OF WAR:
TEMPLAR ASSAULT
The Templar brethren represent the martial traditions of the VII Legion at their most aggressive.
Where other Imperial Fists formations hold the line or break fortifications through methodical siegecraft, a Templar assault is a direct application of overwhelming force intended to destroy the enemy in close combat.
EFFECTS
TEMPLAR HOST
Templar Brethren Squads may be selected as Troops choices.
They may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
CRUSADING ASSAULT
During an Assault phase in which a Templar Brethren Squad charged after disembarking from a vehicle with the Assault Vehicle special rule during the same player turn, the squad gains the Furious Charge special rule. In addition, its normal charge distance is increased from 6" to 7" for that Assault phase.
SWORDS OF THE LEGION
During the first round of a close combat in which a Templar Brethren Squad charged, models in that squad may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 with:
• Rending Weapons
• Power Weapons
• Relic Blades
• other weapons specifically stated to count as swords
ASSAULT TRANSPORTS
A Templar Brethren Squad may select one of the following as a Dedicated Transport at its normal points cost:
• Land Raider Phobos
• Land Raider Proteus
A Templar Brethren Squad of a size which cannot be carried by either vehicle may instead select a Legion Spartan Assault Tank at its normal points cost.
All normal Transport Capacity restrictions apply.
LIMITATIONS
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Templar Brethren Squads.
The army may include no more than one Fast Attack choice.
The army may not include a Fortification.
The army's Warlord must be equipped with a Power Weapon, Rending Weapon, Relic Blade or another sword-like close-combat weapon which ignores Armour Saves.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r64-if-disciplined" name="Disciplined Fire" hidden="false">
                  <description>When an Imperial Fists unit makes a First Fire or Overwatch shooting attack, models in the unit may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when firing Bolters, Bolt Pistols, Combi-Bolters, Storm Bolters, Heavy Bolters, or the bolter component of a Combi-weapon.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r64-if-fortification" name="Fortification Masters" hidden="false">
                  <description>Imperial Fists models receive +1 to Armour Penetration rolls against Fortifications, Buildings, Bunkers and other immobile structures with an Armour Value. A non-vehicle Imperial Fists unit occupying a friendly Fortification or Bunker gains Stubborn; this provides no benefit in an enemy Fortification. If the Imperial Fists are defenders in a mission that permits Fortifications or Obstacles, they may place D3 additional 6-inch sections of razor wire or tank traps wholly within their deployment zone.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r64-if-blind-risk" name="Blind to the Risk" hidden="false">
                  <description>In a mission with variable game length, when the battle would normally end, the opposing player may demand that one additional complete game turn be played. After that turn the battle ends automatically. This has no effect if the mission already ended because a specific objective or action was completed.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="VIII Legion — Night Lords" id="legion-viii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-viii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)" id="legion-viii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Night Lords. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Night Lords). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Night Lords — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-viii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
Lords of the Night
All models with the Legiones Astartes (Night Lords) special rule gain Night Vision. Night Lords retain exclusive access to the Stealth Adept Veteran Skill as described in the Armoury.
Terror Made Manifest
Whenever a non-vehicle Night Lords unit completely destroys an enemy unit in close combat, including by Sweeping Advance, it becomes Terrifying until the end of its next Assault phase.
A Terrifying unit gains Fear. In addition, if it charges an enemy unit that it outnumbers, every model in the Night Lords unit gains +1 Attack for the first round of that combat. This bonus is not cumulative.
Masters of the Terror Assault
Night Lords units arriving by Deep Strike may re-roll the Scatter die.
Night Lords units arriving by Outflank may re-roll the roll used to determine which table edge they arrive from.”
Terror Assault
A Night Lords army may exchange two Heavy Support selections for one additional Fast Attack selection.
The standard Force Organisation Chart therefore becomes:
4 Fast Attack / 1 Heavy Support
NIGHT LORDS ARMOURY
The VIII Legion makes extensive use of weapons and equipment intended as much to terrify its victims as to destroy them. Grisly trophies, oversized chain weapons and specialised infiltration equipment are common amongst the warriors of Nostramo.
NOSTRAMAN CHAINGLAIVE — 10 POINTS
Any Night Lords Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Nostraman Chainglaive for +10 points. Other Night Lords units may gain access to Nostraman Chainglaives through their individual army list entries.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Nostraman Chainglaive | User +1 | Rending, Two-Handed
The Nostraman Chainglaive does not count as a Power Weapon.
TROPHIES OF JUDGEMENT — 10 POINTS
Any Night Lords Independent Character or squad Sergeant may purchase Trophies of Judgement for +10 points. Enemy units with one or more models within 8" of one or more models equipped with Trophies of Judgement suffer -1 Leadership. The effects of multiple Trophies of Judgement are not cumulative. Friendly models are never affected.
Where an entire squad is specifically stated to be equipped with Trophies of Judgement, measure the 8" range from any model in that
squad. The squad counts as a single source of the Leadership penalty.
STEALTH ADEPT
A Night Lords Independent Character may purchase Stealth Adept for +5 points. Any Night Lords Infantry or Jump Infantry unit may purchase Stealth Adept for +1 point per model. Every model in the unit must purchase the upgrade. Models with Stealth Adept gain the Stealth special rule as presented in ProHammer Classic. Models mounted on Bikes or Jetbikes, models wearing any form of Terminator Armour, Dreadnoughts and Vehicles may not purchase Stealth Adept. An Independent Character joining a unit with Stealth Adept must also possess Stealth Adept. Otherwise the unit may not benefit from the upgrade while that character remains attached.
KRAKEN LIGHT BOLTS — 10 POINTS PER UNIT
A Legion Tactical Squad or Legion Veteran Squad may purchase Kraken Light Bolts for +10 points per unit. Terror Squads may also purchase Kraken Light Bolts where stated in their army list entry.
Kraken Light Bolts may be used with Bolters, Combi-Bolters, Twin-linked Bolters and the Bolter component of Combi-Weapons. When firing Kraken Light Bolts, those weapons are treated as AP4.
Kraken Light Bolts may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition or any other ammunition upgrade. A Legion Tactical Squad may not use Fury of the Legion during a Shooting phase in which it fires Kraken Light Bolts.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Night Lords unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for
+15 points per unit. A Night Lords Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +10 points. A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders gains the Deep Strike special rule and may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit Deep Strike.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
NIGHT LORDS RITE OF WAR:
TERROR ASSAULT
The Terror Assault is the favoured method of war of the VIII Legion: a sudden offensive conducted beneath artificial darkness, with enemy communications disrupted and rapid assault formations descending upon isolated positions before a coherent defence can be organised.
EFFECTS
COVER OF DARKNESS
The first Battle Round is fought using the Night Fighting rules. At the beginning of the second Battle Round, roll a D6. On a 3+, Night Fighting remains in effect for the second Battle Round. If Night Fighting remained in effect during the second Battle Round,
roll again at the beginning of the third Battle Round. On a 6, Night Fighting remains in effect for the third Battle Round.
Night Fighting automatically ends at the beginning of the fourth Battle Round. Night Lords units benefit from their normal Night Vision special rule
during these turns.
TERROR FORMATIONS
Night Raptor Squads may be selected as Troops choices. Terror Squads may also be selected as Troops choices once their unit entry is included in the Night Lords army list. Both units may fulfil compulsory Troops selections. At least one of the Detachment's compulsory Troops selections must be a Night Raptor Squad or Terror Squad.
TERROR ATTACK
Whenever the opposing player makes Reserve rolls, after all of those rolls have been made, the Night Lords player may force one successful Reserve roll to be re-rolled. The second result must be accepted. A die may never be re-rolled more than once.
RAPID STRIKE FORCE
The Detachment modifies the Standard Force Organisation Chart as follows:
Fast Attack: 0–4
Heavy Support: 0–1
All other Force Organisation limits remain unchanged.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must include at least one Night Raptor Squad or Terror Squad.
The Detachment may include no more than one Heavy Support choice.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
NIGHT LORDS RITE OF WAR:
HORROR CULT
Some formations of the VIII Legion abandoned even the pretence of disciplined terror warfare, becoming predatory cults of murder whose commanders measured victory in screams and mutilated corpses. The Night Raptors were amongst the most infamous of these formations, descending upon isolated prey in great packs and competing for the most spectacular kill.
EFFECTS
RAPTOR CULT
Night Raptor Squads may be selected as Troops choices. Night Raptor Squads may fulfil compulsory Troops selections. At least one of the Detachment's compulsory Troops selections must be a Night Raptor Squad.
BEYOND JUDGEMENT
Any Night Lords Infantry or Jump Infantry squad may purchase Trophies of Judgement for +25 points per unit.
If purchased in this manner, every model in the unit is treated as being equipped with Trophies of Judgement. Measure the 8" Leadership penalty from any model in the squad. In addition, a unit equipped with Trophies of Judgement in this manner
gains the Fear special rule. The Leadership penalties caused by multiple sources of Trophies of Judgement remain non-cumulative.
VOX-SCREAM BROADCAST
Once per battle, at the beginning of any Night Lords player turn, the Night Lords player may declare a Vox-Scream Broadcast. Until the beginning of the next Night Lords player turn, all enemy units suffer -1 Leadership. This modifier may be combined with the penalty caused by Trophies of
Judgement.
THE SCENT OF BLOOD
A non-Vehicle Night Lords unit using this Rite must declare a charge during its Assault phase if:
• it is normally eligible to charge; and
• at least one enemy unit is within its current charge distance; and
• that enemy unit is a legal charge target under the normal ProHammer rules.
If several eligible enemy units are present, the Night Lords player may choose which one is charged. A unit is never required to declare an illegal charge.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be used by a Traitor Night Lords Detachment.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
A Night Lords unit using this Rite may not voluntarily withdraw from
close combat.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r71-nl-legion-0" name="Lords of the Night" hidden="false">
                  <description>All models with the Legiones Astartes (Night Lords) special rule gain Night Vision. Night Lords retain exclusive access to the Stealth Adept Veteran Skill as described in the Night Lords Armoury.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r71-nl-legion-1" name="Terror Made Manifest" hidden="false">
                  <description>Whenever a non-vehicle Night Lords unit completely destroys an enemy unit in close combat, including by Sweeping Advance, it becomes Terrifying until the end of its next Assault phase. A Terrifying unit gains Fear. In addition, if it charges an enemy unit that it outnumbers, every model in the Night Lords unit gains +1 Attack for the first round of that combat. This bonus is not cumulative.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r71-nl-legion-2" name="Masters of the Terror Assault" hidden="false">
                  <description>Night Lords units arriving by Deep Strike may re-roll the Scatter die. Night Lords units arriving by Outflank may re-roll the roll used to determine which table edge they arrive from.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r71-nl-legion-3" name="Terror Assault" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Night Lords army exchanges two Heavy Support selections for one additional Fast Attack selection. Using the Standard Force Organisation Chart this is 0–4 Fast Attack and 0–1 Heavy Support.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="IX Legion — Blood Angels" id="legion-ix" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-ix-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule id="r74-ba-leg-angels" name="Angels of Death" hidden="false">
                  <description>During an Assault phase in which a Blood Angels model charges, it gains +1 Weapon Skill until the end of that Assault phase. This may combine with other Weapon Skill modifiers. Friendly Imperial Army or Imperial Militia units with at least one model within 6 inches of a Blood Angels unit receive +1 Leadership, to a maximum of 10; this Leadership bonus is not cumulative.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r74-ba-leg-descent" name="Descent of Angels" hidden="false">
                  <description>When a Blood Angels Jump Infantry unit deploys using Deep Strike, the controlling player may re-roll the Scatter die and any dice rolled for scatter distance. The entire result must be re-rolled and the second result accepted.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="r74-ba-leg-vengeance" name="Vengeance of a Fallen Angel" hidden="false">
                  <description>Whenever a friendly Blood Angels Character is slain, every friendly non-vehicle Blood Angels unit with at least one model able to draw line of sight to the Character’s final position is affected until the end of the following Blood Angels player turn: +1 Attack, -1 Leadership, and it must charge the nearest enemy unit it can legally charge. Units already engaged still receive +1 Attack. The effect is not cumulative; another qualifying death extends its duration.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="X Legion — Iron Hands" id="legion-x" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-x-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Iron Hands)" id="legion-x-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Iron Hands. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Iron Hands). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Iron Hands — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-x-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
WISDOM OF THE OMNISSIAH
The Iron Hands place extraordinary faith in machinery and those who understand its mysteries, fighting with renewed determination beneath the guidance of their artificers.
A non-vehicle Iron Hands unit with at least one model within 6" of a friendly model equipped with a Servo-Arm gains:
• Counter-Attack
• Feel No Pain (6+)
These benefits last only while the unit remains within 6" of an eligible model.
Multiple Servo-Arms provide no additional benefit.
IMPLACABLE ADVANCE
The Iron Hands advance with mechanical determination, largely unmoved by fear or suppressive fire but unwilling to abandon formation in pursuit of a broken foe. Iron Hands units may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests. However, Iron Hands units may never make a Sweeping Advance after winning a combat and may only Consolidate instead.
MORE MASCHINE THAN MAN
Iron Hands Characters and Veteran Sergeants may purchase Bionics for 5 points. Any Iron Hands unit consisting wholly of Infantry may purchase Bionics for +3 points per model. Iron Hands models with Bionics successfully recover on a roll of 5+ rather than 6+.
IRON HANDS ARMOURY
The armouries of the X Legion reflect its close ties to the Mechanicum and its contempt for the weakness of flesh. Extensive augmetics, cybernetic systems, graviton weapons and self-repairing vehicle technologies are commonplace amongst the warriors of Medusa.
SERVO-ARM — 30 POINTS
Any Iron Hands model with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Servo-Arm for +30 points, even if the model is not normally permitted to select Techmarine equipment.
A model equipped with a Jump Pack may not purchase a Servo-Arm.
MECHADENDRITES — 15 POINTS
Any Iron Hands Independent Character or Sergeant may purchase Mechadendrites for +15 points.
Once during each phase, the bearer may re-roll one failed Armour Save. This cannot be used to re-roll an Invulnerable Save or Cover Save. The second result must be accepted.
DANGEROUS WEAPONRY
Whenever an Iron Hands model may purchase a Flamer, it may instead purchase a Graviton Gun for +15 points.
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Type
Graviton Gun | 18" | Special | 4 | Heavy 1, Blast, Concussive, Graviton
The Graviton Gun follows the normal Graviton rules presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List and ProHammer Classic.
SPLINTER BOLTS — 5 POINTS PER UNIT
Any Iron Hands Infantry unit equipped with Bolters may purchase Splinter Bolts for +5 points per unit. When firing Splinter Bolts, wounds caused by the unit's Bolters ignore Feel No Pain.
For this purpose, Bolters include Bolters, Combi-Bolters, Twin-linked Bolters and the Bolter component of Combi-Weapons.
Splinter Bolts may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition or another ammunition upgrade. A Legion Tactical Squad may not use Fury of the Legion during a Shooting phase in which it fires Splinter Bolts.
ALBIAN POWER GLADIUS — 10 POINTS
Any Iron Hands Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase an Albian Power Gladius for +10 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Albian Power Gladius | User | Rending (5+)
Rending (5+): The Albian Power Gladius follows the normal ProHammer rules for Rending, except that the effect is triggered on a natural To Wound roll of 5 or 6 rather than only on a 6. Against Vehicles, Rending is still triggered only by a natural Armour Penetration roll of 6.
BLESSED AUTOSIMULACRA — 10 POINTS
Any Iron Hands Vehicle may purchase Blessed Autosimulacra for +10 points.
At the beginning of the Iron Hands Movement phase, select one Weapon Destroyed or Immobilised result currently affecting the Vehicle and roll a D6. On a 6, that result is repaired.
A repaired weapon may fire normally and a repaired Immobilised Vehicle may move normally. Only one repair attempt may be made by each Vehicle per turn. Destroyed Vehicles cannot repair themselves.
IRON FATHER — +25 POINTS
Any Iron Hands Forge Lord Consul may be further upgraded to an Iron Father for +25 points.
Wargear:
• Iron Halo
• Bionics
Special Rules:
• Rites of Battle
The Iron Father retains all rules, wargear and options of a normalForge Lord Consul.
RITES OF BATTLE
The Iron Father and any Iron Hands unit he has joined may re-roll failed Morale tests. The second result must be accepted.
IRON HANDS RITE OF WAR:
THE HEAD OF THE GORGON
The Head of the Gorgon is one of the characteristic battle doctrines of the X Legion. The enemy is fixed against an implacable battle line while armoured reserves manoeuvre around its flanks, closing the jaws of the trap in a storm of mechanised firepower.
EFFECTS
GROUND OF CHOICE
All Iron Hands Infantry units gain the Stubborn special rule while at least half of the unit's surviving models are within the Iron Hands deployment zone.
RELICS OF WAR
All Iron Hands Vehicles in the Detachment receive Blessed Autosimulacra at no additional points cost.
SCIONS OF IRON
Any Iron Hands Infantry unit of ten models or fewer which may normally select a Rhino as a Dedicated Transport may instead select a Land Raider Phobos or Land Raider Proteus as a Dedicated Transport at its normal points cost.
All normal Transport Capacity restrictions apply.
ARMOURED ENCIRCLEMENT
Iron Hands Vehicles with the Tank unit type gain the Outflank special rule if placed in Reserve.
A Dedicated Transport carrying a unit may Outflank together with its passengers. The Transport and embarked unit are treated as a single Reserve entry for this purpose.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment may include no more than one Fast Attack choice.
The Detachment may include no more than one Consul, excluding Forge Lords.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment drawn from another Space Marine Legion.
IRON HANDS RITE OF WAR:
COMPANY OF BITTER IRON
After the massacre at Isstvan V, many Iron Hands renounced their former Clan and Company markings and gathered into formations of Medusan Immortals, seeking vengeance against the Traitors and redemption through death in battle.
EFFECTS
COMPANY OF IMMORTALS
Medusan Immortal Squads may be selected as Troops choices and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
At least one compulsory Troops choice in the Detachment must be a Medusan Immortal Squad.
IMMORTAL HATRED
All units in the Detachment with the Legiones Astartes (Iron Hands) special rule gain Hatred against Traitor forces.
For the purposes of this rule, a Traitor force is any army or unit specifically designated as Traitor by the mission, campaign or army list being used.
BITTER DUTY
A Medusan Immortal Squad gains the Fearless special rule while the majority of its surviving models are within the enemy deployment zone.
NO DEATH WITHOUT PURPOSE
Whenever a Medusan Immortal Squad is completely destroyed while the majority of its models were within the enemy deployment zone immediately before its destruction, every friendly Iron Hands unit within 6" may immediately re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning test it is required to make as a result of that destruction.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Loyalist Iron Hands Detachment.
The army may not include an Allied Detachment.
The army may not include Ferrus Manus.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XII Legion — World Eaters" id="legion-xii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (World Eaters)" id="legion-xii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is World Eaters. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (World Eaters). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="World Eaters — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
BLOOD FRENZY
The World Eaters throw themselves into close combat with a violence unmatched amongst the Legiones Astartes.
World Eaters Infantry, Bike, Jump Infantry and Dreadnought models gain +1 Attack during an Assault phase in which they charged.
This bonus only applies during the first round of that close combat.
Whenever a World Eaters unit wins a close combat, it gains the Rage special rule for the remainder of the battle.
For the purposes of this rule, use the ProHammer 3rd–5th Edition version of Rage.
A World Eaters unit which wins a close combat must Pursue a retreating enemy whenever it is permitted to do so.
If no Pursuit is possible because the enemy was completely destroyed, the unit must Consolidate as directly as possible towards the nearest enemy unit.
WORLD EATERS ARMOURY
The armouries of the XII Legion reflect the gladiatorial traditions of Nuceria and the brutal preferences of Angron's sons. Chainaxes and specialised pit weapons are favoured over more elegant arms, intended to inflict catastrophic wounds at close quarters.
CHAINAXE — 4 POINTS
Any World Eaters model eligible to carry a Close Combat Weapon may replace it with a Chainaxe for +4 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Chainaxe | User | Chainaxe
CHAINAXE
An Armour Save better than 4+ is reduced to 4+ against wounds caused by a Chainaxe. Armour Saves of 4+ or worse are unaffected. Invulnerable Saves are unaffected.
CAEDERE WEAPON — 15 POINTS
Any World Eaters Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Caedere Weapon for +15 points. Rampager Squads may gain access to Caedere Weapons through their individual army list entry.
Caedere Weapons encompass the many axes, hooked blades, meteor hammers and other gladiatorial weapons used within the XII Legion's fighting pits.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Caedere Weapon | User +1 | Rending
A Caedere Weapon counts as a one-handed close-combat weapon. It does not count as a Power Weapon.
WORLD EATERS RITE OF WAR:
BERSERKER ASSAULT
A Berserker Assault commits the XII Legion to a single overwhelming attack, massed assault formations racing ahead of their support elements to close with the enemy before disciplined resistance can be organised.
EFFECTS
THE RED HAND
Rampager Squads may be selected as Troops choices and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
Legion Assault Squads may fulfil compulsory Troops selections normally.
HEADLONG ASSAULT
World Eaters Infantry and Jump Infantry units gain the Fleet special rule.
A unit with Fleet may charge after making an Advance move, following the normal ProHammer rules.
WEAPONS OF THE PITS
World Eaters models in Legion Assault Squads and Rampager Squads may purchase Chainaxes for +2 points per model instead of the normal +4 points.
BLOOD FORWARD
A non-Vehicle World Eaters unit must declare a charge during its Assault phase if it is normally eligible to charge and at least one enemy unit is within its current charge distance.
If more than one legal target is available, the World Eaters player may choose which unit is charged.
LIMITATIONS
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Legion Assault Squads or Rampager Squads.
At least one compulsory Troops choice must be a Rampager Squad.
The army's Warlord must be equipped with a Chainaxe, Caedere Weapon, Rending Weapon, Power Weapon or another close-combat weapon.
The Detachment may include no more than one Heavy Support choice.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
WORLD EATERS RITE OF WAR:
THE CRIMSON PATH
From the earliest years of the Great Crusade, the XII Legion was willing to accept casualties that other Legions would consider catastrophic. As the World Eaters descended further into madness, entire formations became capable of enduring horrific wounds for the few moments necessary to reach the enemy and drag them into death.
EFFECTS
FORLORN HOPE
World Eaters Infantry models gain Feel No Pain (5+) while they are within the enemy deployment zone.
If a model already possesses Feel No Pain, improve its Feel No Pain roll by one step while it remains within the enemy deployment zone, to a maximum of 3+.
UNTO DEATH
World Eaters Independent Characters gain the It Will Not Die special rule while they are within the enemy deployment zone.
If a Character already possesses It Will Not Die, it instead regains a lost Wound on a roll of 4+ while within the enemy deployment zone.
THE PATH MUST END IN BLOOD
At the end of the battle, if the World Eaters have no surviving non-Vehicle unit at least partially within the enemy deployment zone, the opposing player gains an additional 150 Victory Points.
In addition, if the opposing army has completely destroyed more World Eaters units than the World Eaters have completely destroyed enemy units, the opposing player gains an additional 150 Victory Points.
These penalties only apply in missions using Victory Points.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment may not include units with the Slow and Purposeful special rule.
The Detachment may not include Immobile units.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment drawn from another Space Marine Legion.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XIII Legion — Ultramarines" id="legion-xiii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xiii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)" id="legion-xiii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Ultramarines. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Ultramarines — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xiii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
CODEX ASTARTES
The XIII Legion possesses an extraordinarily flexible and disciplined command structure, allowing its forces to divide and reorganise rapidly as battlefield conditions demand.
A Legion Tactical Squad consisting of exactly ten models may be divided into two Combat Squads of five models each.
This decision is made before deployment.
The Sergeant, specialist weapons, heavy weapons, Legion Vexilla and Nuncio Vox may be divided between the two Combat Squads as the Ultramarines player wishes.
After being divided, each Combat Squad counts as a separate unit for deployment, Morale, casualties, scoring and all other purposes.
For Victory Points, each Combat Squad is worth half the original unit's total points value. Any remaining fraction is assigned to the squad containing the Sergeant.
If the original Tactical Squad purchased a Dedicated Transport, it must be assigned to one of the Combat Squads. Only that Combat Squad may begin the battle embarked within it.
FLEXIBLE COMMAND STRUCTURE
The Ultramarines maintain an unusually large and highly organised officer corps capable of directing complex operations without loss of cohesion.
An Ultramarines Detachment may include up to four HQ selections.
The normal limitation on models with Master of the Legion still applies.
In addition, an Ultramarines army begins the battle with one additional Strategy Point.
This Strategy Point follows all normal ProHammer rules.
ULTRAMARINES ARMOURY
The armouries of the XIII Legion reflect the ordered and pragmatic nature of the Ultramarines. Rather than favouring esoteric or excessively specialised weapons, the Legion prizes equipment of proven effectiveness, refined through centuries of warfare and manufactured to exacting standards throughout the Five Hundred Worlds.
LEGATINE AXE — 20 POINTS
Any Ultramarines Independent Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Legatine Axe for +20 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Legatine Axe | User +1 | Power Weapon, Two-Handed
The Legatine Axe is a precisely balanced power weapon designed to combine the cutting force of an axe with the speed and control demanded by the warriors of Macragge.
MANTLE OF ULTRAMAR — 20 POINTS
An Ultramarines Praetor equipped with Artificer Armour may exchange it for a Mantle of Ultramar for +20 points.
A Mantle of Ultramar grants a 2+ Armour Save and Feel No Pain (5+). In addition, the bearer is immune to the effects of the Blind special rule.
This protection applies only to the bearer. A unit joined by the bearer may still be affected by Blind normally.
BREACHER POWER WEAPONS — +5 POINTS PER MODEL
Any model in an Ultramarines Legion Breacher Siege Squad may replace its Bolter with a Power Weapon for +5 points.
A model which replaces its Bolter in this manner may not also select another weapon which replaces its Bolter from the squad's Specialist Weapons options.
ULTRAMARINES RITE OF WAR:
THE LOGOS LECTORA
The Logos Lectora is the battlefield application of the immense body of tactical theory compiled by the XIII Legion. Through disciplined command, precise communication and carefully coordinated formations, an Ultramarines force may alter its method of war as the tactical situation demands.
EFFECTS
TACTICAL COMMAND
At the beginning of each Ultramarines player turn, choose one of the following three commands: Full March, Hold Fast or Retribution Strike.
The chosen command applies until the beginning of the next Ultramarines player turn. Only one command may be active at a time.
FULL MARCH
All Ultramarines non-Vehicle units may re-roll the D6 used to determine the additional distance of an Advance Move. The second result must be accepted.
HOLD FAST
Ultramarines non-Vehicle units which remain stationary during their Movement phase may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when resolving First Fire or Overwatch Fire.
In addition, any Snap Fire attacks made by such a unit hit on a 5+ instead of the normal 6+. Ultramarines Dreadnoughts may also benefit from this command if they remained stationary.
RETRIBUTION STRIKE
All Ultramarines non-Vehicle units gain the Counter-Attack special rule.
An Ultramarines Dreadnought which was not already engaged and is successfully charged instead gains +1 Attack during that Assault phase.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must take one additional compulsory HQ choice. This additional choice must be a Legion Master of Signals Consul or a Damocles Command Rhino.
The Detachment must take one additional compulsory Troops choice.
The Detachment may not include more Vehicles with the Tank or Flyer type than it includes Infantry units.
Units in the Detachment may not deploy using Infiltrate or enter play using Deep Strike. Normal Reserves may still be used.
Units which are required to enter play using Deep Strike, such as Legion Drop Pods, may not be selected.
ULTRAMARINES RITE OF WAR:
VIGIL OPERTII MISSION
The Vigil Opertii are one of the less celebrated instruments of Ultramar's rule, employing veteran Legionaries and carefully selected mortal auxiliaries in counter-insurgency, reconnaissance and internal security operations throughout the Five Hundred Worlds.
EFFECTS
VIGIL AUXILIA
All Infantry units in the army's allied Imperialis Militia Detachment gain the Infiltrate special rule.
SACRED DUTY
All Infantry units in the allied Imperialis Militia Detachment gain Implacable Advance and count as Scoring Units regardless of their normal battlefield role.
OVERSEERS
Ultramarines Legion Reconnaissance Squads lose the Support Squad special rule and may therefore be selected to fulfil compulsory Troops choices.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be used by a Loyalist Ultramarines Detachment.
The army must include an Allied Detachment drawn from the Imperialis Militia &amp; Cults Army List.
The Allied Detachment must possess both the Gene-crafted and Warrior Elite Provenances of War.
The Allied Detachment may not include Inducted Levy Squads.
The Ultramarines Detachment must include a Legion Vigilator Consul.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XIV Legion — Death Guard" id="legion-xiv" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xiv-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Death Guard)" id="legion-xiv-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Death Guard. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Death Guard). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Death Guard — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xiv-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
Steady Assault
The Death Guard are trained to advance relentlessly on foot, maintaining fire even through the most hostile terrain.
All Death Guard Infantry gain True Grit and Move Through Cover.
True Grit: Models may count their bolter as a bolt pistol in close combat and may therefore gain an additional Attack if equipped with a second pistol or close combat weapon. However, a model using its bolter in this manner does not gain the bonus Attack for charging.
Resilience of Barbarus
All Death Guard models have Feel No Pain (4+) against wounds caused by Poisoned weapons.
Footslogging Killers
A Death Guard army may take only 0–1 selection in total from the following units:
Land Speeder Squadron, Attack Bike Squadron, Bike Squadron.
DEATH GUARD ARMOURY
The XIV Legion maintains extensive stocks of proscribed chemical, radiological and biological weapons. Mortarion's sons have little concern for the long-term consequences of such weapons, regarding them simply as another means by which an enemy position may be reduced.
MANREAPER — 20 POINTS
Any Death Guard Sergeant or Character permitted to select weapons from the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Manreaper.
A Manreaper is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. At the beginning of each Assault phase in which the bearer is engaged in close combat, roll a D3. The bearer gains that many additional Attacks until the end of that Assault phase. If the bearer directs all of his attacks against a single enemy Independent Character or other separately targetable model, he gains only +1 Attack instead. The bearer receives no additional Attack for fighting with a second close-combat weapon.
ALCHEM FLAMER
A Death Guard model equipped with a Flamer or Heavy Flamer may replace it with an Alchem Flamer at no additional cost. A model permitted to select a Combi-flamer may instead select a Combi-Alchem Flamer for +4 points in addition to the normal cost of the Combi-flamer. The Alchem Flamer component follows the normal rules for Combi-weapons.
Alchem Flamer | Template | 2 | 5 | Assault 1, Poisoned (3+)
DEATH GUARD RITE OF WAR:
THE REAPING
The Reaping is one of the characteristic attack formations of the XIV Legion. Heavy infantry and fire-support units advance in a relentless column, purging shattered cities and fortified battlefields through weight of fire and remorseless attrition.
EFFECTS
SUPERIOR FIREPOWER
Legion Veteran Squads and Legion Heavy Support Squads may be selected as non-compulsory Troops choices.
They may not fulfil compulsory Troops selections unless another rule specifically permits them to do so.
IMPLACABLE
All Death Guard Infantry units gain the Move Through Cover special rule.
This includes models wearing any form of Terminator Armour.
DARK ARSENAL
Any Death Guard Character or Independent Character may purchase Rad Grenades for +10 points.
Rad Grenades follow the normal rules presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List.
LIMITATIONS
Units in the Detachment may not make Advance Moves.
Vehicles in the Detachment may not move Flat Out.
Units in the Detachment may not deploy using Deep Strike. Units which are required to deploy using Deep Strike may not be selected.
The normal Death Guard restriction on Fast Attack choices from Footslogging Killers continues to apply.
DEATH GUARD RITE OF WAR:
CREEPING DEATH
As the Horus Heresy progressed, the Death Guard unleashed ever greater quantities of forbidden chemical and biological weapons. Entire regions were reduced to poisoned wastelands through which the warriors of the XIV Legion advanced seemingly untouched.
EFFECTS
MIST-CLAD
Death Guard Infantry models in open ground receive a 5+ Cover Save against shooting attacks provided there is no enemy model within 12".
This does not improve an existing Cover Save.
BIO-PHAGE BOMBARDMENT
After both armies have deployed, including Scouts and Infiltrators, roll a D6 for every piece of terrain representing a wood or jungle.
On a 4+, that terrain is reduced to a fetid chemical mire for the remainder of the battle.
Any Cover Save provided by that terrain is worsened by 1. For example, a 4+ Cover Save becomes 5+, while a 6+ Cover Save is lost.
The terrain also counts as Dangerous Terrain to all models except models with the Legiones Astartes (Death Guard) special rule.
TOXIN WEAPONS
Frag Missiles fired by Death Guard models are resolved at Strength 5 instead of Strength 4.
In addition, Death Guard Frag Grenades used against Vehicles have Strength 5 + D6 Armour Penetration instead of the normal Strength 4 + D6.
All other rules for Frag Grenades and Frag Missiles remain unchanged.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Traitor Death Guard Detachment.
The Detachment must include at least one Legion Heavy Support Squad whose Sergeant has been upgraded to a Siege Breaker.
In missions which designate one player as the Attacker and the other as the Defender, the Death Guard must be the Attacker.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XV Legion — Thousand Sons" id="legion-xv" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xv-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)" id="legion-xv-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Thousand Sons. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Thousand Sons — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xv-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
SORCERERS OF PROSPERO
The Thousand Sons possess an unparalleled concentration of psychic talent amongst the Legiones Astartes, and the study of the Warp permeates every level of the Legion.
All Thousand Sons Independent Characters are Psykers.
Unless they already possess a higher Psychic Mastery Level, they count as Psyker (Mastery Level 1).
A Thousand Sons Praetor instead counts as Psyker (Mastery Level 2).
Thousand Sons Psykers may select their psychic powers from the following ProHammer Psychic Disciplines:
• Biomancy
• Divination
• Pyromancy
• Telekinesis
• Telepathy
The number of powers known and which may be invoked is determined by the Psyker's Mastery Level and the normal ProHammer psychic rules.
A Thousand Sons Librarian Consul follows these rules normally. Activating a Force Weapon counts as the use of a psychic power.
A Psyker may not use the same psychic power more than once during the same player turn.
THE PROSPERINE CULTS
The warriors of the Thousand Sons were organised according to the great psychic Cults of Prospero, each devoted to the mastery of a particular aspect of the psychic arts. Every Thousand Sons Infantry unit and Independent Character must be assigned to one of the following Prosperine Cults when the army is selected:
• Pavoni
• Raptora
• Corvidae
• Athanaeans
• Pyrae
The chosen Cult must be recorded on the army roster. Every unit receives the normal Cult Arcana of its chosen Cult.
A model or unit may normally belong to only one Prosperine Cult. An Independent Character retains his own Cult when joining a unit belonging to another Cult. Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery are not conferred between the Independent Character and the unit unless specifically stated otherwise.
CULT MASTERY
A unit with the Psyker or Brotherhood of Psykers special rule has fully manifested the teachings of its Prosperine Cult and additionally receives the Cult Mastery benefit listed for that Cult.
Cult Mastery does not require a Psychic Test and does not count as the use of a psychic power.
PAVONI — QUICKBLOOD
The Pavoni practise mastery over the biological processes of the body, accelerating muscle, nerve and reflex far beyond even the already superhuman limits of the Legiones Astartes.
CULT ARCANA
Pavoni units gain the Fleet special rule.
CULT MASTERY
A Pavoni Psyker or Psychic Brotherhood also gains the Crusader special rule.
RAPTORA — KINE SHIELDS
The Raptora manipulate telekinetic force, surrounding themselves with barriers capable of deflecting incoming fire.
CULT ARCANA
Models in a Raptora unit gain a 6+ Invulnerable Save against shooting attacks.
This does not improve an existing Invulnerable Save.
CULT MASTERY
Models in a Raptora Psyker unit or Psychic Brotherhood instead gain a 5+ Invulnerable Save against shooting attacks.
If a model already possesses an Invulnerable Save, improve that save by 1 against shooting attacks instead, to a maximum of 4+.
In addition, the unit improves any Cover Save it receives against shooting attacks by 1, to a maximum of 3+.
These benefits have no effect in close combat.
CORVIDAE — PRECOGNITIVE STRIKE
The Corvidae glimpse fragments of possible futures, allowing them to anticipate the actions of their enemies before they occur.
CULT ARCANA
When a Corvidae unit resolves a First Fire shooting attack, it may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1.
This bonus applies to all ranged weapons fired by the unit as part of that First Fire attack.
CULT MASTERY
A Corvidae Psyker unit or Psychic Brotherhood may also re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when making:
• Overwatch attacks
• Return Fire attacks
• Stand &amp; Shoot attacks
ATHANAEANS — DISCIPLINE OF THE MIND
The Athanaeans possess extraordinary mental discipline and specialise in telepathy, psychic communication and the defence of the mind against outside influence.
CULT ARCANA
Athanaean units gain:
• Stubborn
• Re-roll failed Pinning tests
CULT MASTERY
An Athanaean Psyker unit or Psychic Brotherhood additionally gains the Adamantium Will special rule.
PYRAE — ASHEN BLOW
The Pyrae manipulate heat and psychic flame, surrounding themselves with destructive energies as they close upon the enemy.
CULT ARCANA
Pyrae units gain the Hammer of Wrath special rule.
CULT MASTERY
Close-combat attacks and Flame weapons used by models in a Pyrae Psyker unit or Psychic Brotherhood gain the Soul Blaze special rule.
PSYCHIC BROTHERHOODS
The Thousand Sons routinely gathered their most psychically gifted veterans into circles capable of focusing their abilities through collective discipline.
The following units may purchase the Brotherhood of Psykers special rule for +25 points per squad:
• Legion Veteran Squad
• Legion Terminator Squad
A unit upgraded in this manner counts as a Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 1).
The unit then selects one psychic power from the ProHammer Psychic Discipline associated with its chosen Prosperine Cult, as shown below:
Discipline
Pavoni Biomancy
RaptoraTelekinesis
Corvidae Divination
Athanaeans Telepathy
Pyrae Pyromancy
The unit follows all normal ProHammer rules for Brotherhood of Psykers.
The unit additionally gains the Cult Mastery benefit of its chosen Prosperine Cult.
An Independent Character which joins a Psychic Brotherhood remains a separate Psyker and does not combine its Mastery Level, psychic powers or Psychic Tests with those of the Brotherhood.
PRICE OF KNOWLEDGE
The Thousand Sons maintained an unusually large body of officers, scholars and specialist formations, but the concentration of such irreplaceable warriors carried its own risks.
A Thousand Sons Detachment may include:
• one additional HQ selection;
• one additional Elites selection;
• one fewer Fast Attack selection.
When using the Standard Force Organisation Chart, this gives:
HQ: 1–3
Elites: 0–4
Fast Attack: 0–2
The Thousand Sons player must identify on the army roster which HQ and Elites selections occupy the additional slots.
If Victory Points are being used, each unit selected using an additional HQ or Elites selection awards the opposing player an additional 50 Victory Points if completely destroyed.
SIGNS AND PORTENTS
The psychic communion which gives the Thousand Sons their extraordinary strength also leaves the Legion vulnerable to psychic catastrophe. The Flesh Change is never entirely absent from the thoughts of Magnus' sons.
Whenever a Thousand Sons Psyker or Brotherhood of Psykers suffers one or more Wounds as a result of Perils of the Warp, every friendly non-vehicle unit with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule must immediately take a Pinning test
In addition, if every Thousand Sons Independent Character in the Detachment has been slain, all surviving units with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule:
• suffer -1 Leadership for the remainder of the battle;
• may no longer make Pursuit moves.
THOUSAND SONS ARMOURY
The armouries of the XV Legion combine conventional Legiones Astartes technology with psycho-reactive materials, occult devices and weapons whose operation relies upon the psychic disciplines of Prospero.
PROSPERINE FORCE WEAPON — POWER WEAPON +10 POINTS
Any Thousand Sons model permitted to select a Power Weapon may upgrade that Power Weapon to a Force Weapon for +10 points.
A Prosperine Force Weapon follows the normal rules for Force Weapons.
If a model belonging to a Psychic Brotherhood inflicts one or more unsaved wounds with a Force Weapon, nominate one model in that Brotherhood which inflicted such a wound. The Brotherhood may make a single Psychic Test to activate that model's Force Weapon. If passed, only the unsaved wounds inflicted by that nominated model's Force Weapon become Massive Wounds and inflict D3 Wounds instead.
A Psychic Brotherhood may attempt only one Force Weapon activation during each Assault phase, regardless of how many models in the unit carry Force Weapons.
ARCANE LITANIES — 10 POINTS
Any Thousand Sons Independent Character with Psychic Mastery Level 1 or higher may purchase Arcane Litanies for +10 points.
Once per battle, when the bearer suffers a Wound from Perils of the Warp, it may ignore that Wound. The Psychic Test and psychic power are otherwise resolved normally.
ÆTHER-FIRE CANNON — FREE UPGRADE
Any Thousand Sons model equipped with a Plasma Cannon may upgrade it to an Æther-fire Cannon at no additional points cost.
If a unit contains more than one Plasma Cannon, either all or none of them must be upgraded.
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Æther-fire Cannon | 36" | 7 | 2 | Heavy 1, Blast, Gets Hot, Soul Blaze
ASPHYX SHELLS
A Thousand Sons Independent Character may purchase Asphyx Shells for +10 points. A Legion Veteran Squad or Legion Terminator Squad may purchase Asphyx Shells for +20 points per squad.
Asphyx Shells may be used with Bolt Pistols, Bolters, Combi-Bolters and the Bolter component of Combi-Weapons. Weapons firing Asphyx Shells gain the Shred special rule.
Asphyx Shells may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition or another ammunition upgrade.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Thousand Sons unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit. A Thousand Sons Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase them for +10 points.
A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders gains the Deep Strike special rule and may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit it.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
PROSPERINE ÆTHER-DISC — 30 POINTS
Any Thousand Sons Independent Character wearing Power Armour or Artificer Armour may purchase a Prosperine Æther-Disc for +30 points.
The bearer becomes Jump Infantry and follows all normal ProHammer rules for Jump Infantry. In addition, the bearer gains the Turbo-Boosters and Hammer of Wrath special rules.
ÆTHERIC EVASION
If the bearer moved at least 6" during its preceding Movement phase, enemy models suffer -1 on their To Hit rolls when attacking the bearer in close combat, to a maximum required roll of 6+.
This benefit is lost while the bearer is Falling Back.
A Prosperine Æther-Disc may not be combined with a Jump Pack, Bike, Jetbike or any form of Terminator Armour.
THOUSAND SONS RITE OF WAR:
THE AXIS OF DISSOLUTION
The Axis of Dissolution is a carefully prepared tactical configuration in which the enemy is drawn against positions selected in advance by the Legion's seers, held in place by disciplined resistance and destroyed as the pattern of battle unfolds.
EFFECTS
THE ALEMBIC OF ADAMANT
Thousand Sons units automatically pass Morale and Pinning tests while they have at least one model within 6" of an Objective.
If the mission does not use Objective markers, after deployment zones have been determined the Thousand Sons player may nominate one terrain feature outside the enemy deployment zone. The centre of that terrain feature counts as an Objective for the purposes of this rule only.
THE CAUSTIC OF GRACE
Thousand Sons Infantry units may enter Overwatch even if they moved during their preceding Movement phase, provided they did not Advance.
All other ProHammer requirements for entering Overwatch apply normally.
THE TRANSITION OF VITRIOL
Thousand Sons models may re-roll failed To Hit and To Wound rolls when attacking an enemy unit which is Falling Back.
Against Vehicles affected by a mission-specific retreat or withdrawal rule, re-roll failed Armour Penetration rolls instead of failed To Wound rolls.
LIMITATIONS
Every Troops choice in the Detachment must be taken at its maximum permitted unit size.
The Detachment may not contain more Vehicles with the Tank or Flyer type than it contains Infantry units.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
THOUSAND SONS RITE OF WAR:
THE GUARD OF THE CRIMSON KING
When the most powerful formations of the XV Legion were committed to battle, the Sekhmet and the Legion's greatest sorcerers could be concentrated into a single overwhelming psychic spearhead.
EFFECTS
ASTRAL WARFARE
The first two psychic powers successfully invoked by Thousand Sons Psykers during each player turn are ignored when determining the penalties caused by Disturbance in the Warp.
All other ProHammer psychic rules apply normally.
WREATHED IN LIGHTNING, THEY REND THE VEIL
All Thousand Sons units composed entirely of models wearing Terminator Armour gain Teleportation Transponders at no additional points cost.
Thousand Sons Independent Characters may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +10 points regardless of the armour they wear.
Whenever a unit or Character using these Transponders arrives by Deep Strike, it gains the Fear special rule and may re-roll Invulnerable Save rolls of 1 until the beginning of the next Thousand Sons player turn.
INITIATES OF THE SCARAB
Sekhmet Terminator Cabals may be selected as Troops choices and must fulfil the Detachment's compulsory Troops selections.
THE BIDDING OF THE CRIMSON KING
Magnus the Red may fulfil a compulsory HQ selection when using this Rite and does not occupy a Lord of War selection.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be Magnus the Red, Ahzek Ahriman or a Thousand Sons Praetor.
A Thousand Sons Praetor selected as the Warlord may be upgraded from Mastery Level 2 to Mastery Level 3 for +25 points.
The Detachment may not contain more Vehicle units than units with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment or Fortification.
THOUSAND SONS RITE OF WAR:
THE FELLOWSHIPS OF PROSPERO
The Thousand Sons were organised into great Fellowships whose warriors trained and fought beneath circles of powerful psykers. In some formations entire battle companies acted as extensions of their sorcerous commanders, combining Legion discipline with the collective psychic gifts of Prospero.
EFFECTS
CIRCLES OF INITIATES
A Legion Tactical Squad containing 20 models may purchase Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 1\) for +25 points per squad.
A Tactical Squad upgraded in this manner selects one psychic power from the normal Psychic Disciplines available to Thousand Sons Psykers and gains the Cult Mastery benefit of its chosen Prosperine Cult.
The unit follows all normal ProHammer rules for Brotherhood of Psykers.
FELLOWSHIP VETERANS
Legion Veteran Squads and Legion Terminator Squads purchase Brotherhood of Psykers for +15 points per squad instead of the normal +25 points.
MAGISTER TEMPLI
At the beginning of each Thousand Sons player turn, the Warlord may nominate one friendly Psychic Brotherhood within 12".
Until the beginning of the next Thousand Sons player turn, that Brotherhood may use the Warlord's Leadership when taking Psychic Tests.
This specifically overrides the normal rule preventing a Psychic Brotherhood from using the Leadership of an attached Independent Character.
ORDER OF THE CULTS
Every Psychic Brotherhood in the Detachment must belong to the same Prosperine Cult as at least one Thousand Sons Independent Character in the army.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be a Thousand Sons Psyker.
The Detachment must include at least two Psychic Brotherhoods.
A Legion Tactical Squad may only purchase Brotherhood of Psykers if it contains 20 models.
The Detachment may include no more than one Fast Attack choice.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XVI Legion — Sons of Horus" id="legion-xvi" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xvi-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)" id="legion-xvi-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Sons of Horus. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Sons Of Horus — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xvi-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
CLOSE RANGE BRUTALITY
The Sons of Horus favour overwhelming close-range assaults in which gunfire and blade work become almost indistinguishable.
At the beginning of the Assault phase, a Sons of Horus unit which is otherwise able to charge may fire at the enemy unit it intends to charge.
Models armed with Rapid Fire, Pistol or Assault weapons may fire.
Template weapons may not be used.
These attacks hit only on a 5+, regardless of Ballistic Skill, and never cause Morale or Pinning tests.
Firing in this manner does not prevent the unit from charging, but it must charge the unit it fired upon.
If casualties leave the target outside charge range, or destroy it completely, the Sons of Horus unit may not declare a charge against another enemy unit.
Instead, it moves D6" directly towards the target's current position, or its final position if it was destroyed.
This movement is not a charge and may not bring the unit within 1" of another enemy model.
TIP OF THE SPEAR
The Sons of Horus excel at decapitation strikes and sudden assaults upon the most important point in the enemy line.
Even if the mission does not normally permit Deep Strike, the following may deploy using Deep Strike:
• one Sons of Horus Infantry unit selected from Elites;
• one Sons of Horus Independent Character, either alone or joined by a Command Squad.
These units must begin the battle in Reserve.
PRIDE OF THE WARMASTER
The Sons of Horus possess an arrogance born of countless victories and the favour of the Warmaster himself
At the end of the final scheduled game turn, the opposing player may demand that one additional complete game turn be played.
Roll a D6. On a 4+, one additional complete game turn is played. This roll may only be made once per battle.
This rule does not extend a mission which has already ended because a specific objective or action was completed.
SONS OF HORUS ARMOURY
As the favoured Legion of the Warmaster, the Sons of Horus enjoyed access to enormous reserves of arms and munitions. Alongside these Imperial weapons survived the brutal traditions of Cthonia, where weapons intended for gang warfare and murder remained prized even amongst the Legion's highest officers.
BANESTRIKE AMMUNITION — 5 POINTS PER MODEL
Sons of Horus Seeker Squads, Justaerin Terminator Squads and Independent Characters equipped with a Bolter, Foeblaster Boltgun, Combi-Bolter, Storm Bolter or Combi-Weapon may purchase Banestrike Ammunition for +5 points per eligible model.
Every eligible model in a squad must purchase the upgrade, or none may do so. Models which have replaced their bolt weapon with another weapon neither pay for nor benefit from Banestrike Ammunition.
When firing Banestrike Ammunition, use the following profile where appropriate:
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Banestrike Bolter | 18" | 4 | 4 | Rapid Fire, Banestrike
BANESTRIKE
A natural To Wound roll of 6 made with Banestrike Ammunition is resolved at AP3.
When Banestrike Ammunition is used with a Foeblaster Boltgun, Storm Bolter, Combi-Bolter or the bolter component of a Combi-Weapon, retain the weapon's normal number of shots and firing type, but reduce its range to 18", use AP4 and apply the Banestrike special rule.
Banestrike Ammunition may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition or another ammunition upgrade.
CTHONIAN CULLING BLADE — 10 POINTS
Any Sons of Horus Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Cthonian Culling Blade for +10 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Cthonian Culling Blade | User | Rending (5+)
RENDING (5+)
A Cthonian Culling Blade follows the normal ProHammer rules for Rending, except that the effect is triggered on a natural To Wound roll of 5 or 6.
Against Vehicles, Rending is still triggered only by a natural Armour Penetration roll of 6.
A Cthonian Culling Blade does not count as a Power Weapon.
CHAINAXE — 4 POINTS
Any Sons of Horus Character eligible to select a Close Combat Weapon may instead select a Chainaxe for +4 points.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Chainaxe | User | Chainaxe
A Chainaxe follows the normal rules presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Sons of Horus unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit. A Sons of Horus Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase them for +10 points.
A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders gains the Deep Strike special rule and may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit it.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
SONS OF HORUS RITE OF WAR:
THE LONG MARCH
After Isstvan V, the Sons of Horus formed the spearhead of the Warmaster's advance upon Terra, an all-conquering host that drove relentlessly through the Imperium and swept aside world after world in its path.
EFFECTS
RELENTLESS MARCH
At the beginning of each Sons of Horus player turn, determine the position of the majority of the surviving models in each Sons of Horus Infantry unit. The unit gains the appropriate special rule until the beginning of the next Sons of Horus player turn:
• Within the Sons of Horus deployment zone — Relentless.
• Outside either player's deployment zone — Fleet.
• Within the enemy deployment zone — Crusader.
If a unit is equally divided between two areas, the controlling player chooses which applicable rule it gains.
THE WARMASTER'S PORTION
During the first Sons of Horus player turn, all units in the Detachment may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1.
In addition, Legion Terminator Squads may be selected as non-compulsory Troops choices.
They may not fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Traitor Sons of Horus Detachment.
The Detachment may not include models with the Slow and Purposeful special rule unless they begin the battle embarked aboard a Transport or enter play using Deep Strike.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.
SONS OF HORUS RITE OF WAR:
THE BLACK REAVING
The Black Reaving embodies the Cthonian heritage of the XVI Legion. Rather than engaging the enemy in a single ordered battle line, Reaver companies and supporting formations encircle their prey, isolate individual formations and fall upon them from several directions like the gangs of ancient Cthonia.
EFFECTS
REAVER ONSLAUGHT
Reaver Attack Squads may be selected as Troops choices and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
At least one of the Detachment's compulsory Troops choices must be a Reaver Attack Squad.
CTHONIAN ENCIRCLEMENT
After both armies have been selected, nominate up to two Sons of Horus Infantry units. These units gain the Outflank special rule.
Any Dedicated Transport purchased for one of these units also gains Outflank and enters play together with its passengers.
An Independent Character which begins the battle attached to one of these nominated units may Outflank with it.
When one of the two nominated units enters play, the Sons of Horus player may choose the side table edge from which that unit enters instead of rolling to determine the edge. The other nominated unit follows the normal ProHammer Outflank rules.
LODGE CEREMONY
Once per battle, at the beginning of a Sons of Horus player turn, the Warlord may declare a Lodge Ceremony.
Until the end of that player turn, all non-Vehicle Sons of Horus units gain the Fleet special rule.
CUT THEM APART
During the first round of a close combat, a Sons of Horus unit which charged an enemy unit that was already engaged with another friendly Sons of Horus unit may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1.
This benefit applies only during the player turn in which the unit charged.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must include a Legion Centurion upgraded to a Master of Signals Consul.
At least one compulsory Troops choice must be a Reaver Attack Squad.
The Detachment must include at least as many Fast Attack choices as Heavy Support choices.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XVII Legion — Word Bearers" id="legion-xvii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xvii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)" id="legion-xvii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Word Bearers. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Word Bearers — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xvii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
FANATICAL DEVOTION
The Word Bearers are driven by a religious fervour which allows them to endure hardship and terror through sheer certainty of purpose.
Non-Daemon units with the Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers) special rule may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests.
THE DARK SHEPHERDS
The Word Bearers do not march to war without spiritual leaders to guide their warriors.
A Word Bearers Detachment must include at least one Legion Chaplain Consul or Legion-specific Dark Apostle as an HQ selection.
A character specifically stated to count as a Dark Apostle also fulfils this requirement.
RITUAL OF CONSECRATION
Traitor Word Bearers regard every battlefield as sacred ground upon which blood may be offered to the powers they serve.
When a non-Daemon Word Bearers unit completely destroys an enemy unit during the Assault Phase, it may forgo its Consolidation move.
If it does so, nominate one friendly Daemonic Covenant unit currently in Reserve. That unit may re-roll its next Reserve roll.
Only one Covenant unit may receive this benefit each turn.
This rule has no effect in a Loyalist Word Bearers army.
DAEMONIC COVENANT
The Word Bearers were the first Legion to willingly bind the entities of the Warp to their cause. Through sacrifice and profane ritual, they learned to tear openings in reality through which these creatures could be summoned to war. A Traitor Word Bearers army may include a Daemons of the Ruinstorm Covenant Detachment, selected from the Daemons of the Ruinstorm Army List.
DAEMONS OF THE RUINSTORM COVENANT DETACHMENT
Selection | Allowance
HQ | 0–1
Troops | 1–3
Elites | 0–1
Fast Attack | 0–1
Heavy Support | 0–1
An HQ choice is not compulsory, but at least one Troops choice must be selected.
The Covenant Detachment may cost no more than 25% of the army's total points limit and has no minimum points requirement.
Units are purchased using their normal profiles, options, Dominions and special rules from the Daemons of the Ruinstorm Army List.
The Covenant Detachment counts as the army's Allied Detachment and does not require additional permission to use. A Word Bearers army may not include another Allied Detachment unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Covenant units may not fulfil compulsory selections in the primary Word Bearers Detachment and may not provide the army's Warlord. Word Bearers and Covenant units are treated as Fellow Warriors. Independent Characters from one Detachment may not join units from the other.
DAEMONIC SUMMONING
All units in a Daemonic Covenant Detachment must begin the battle in Reserve.
They may not deploy normally, Infiltrate or Outflank, but instead enter play using the following rules.
When a Covenant unit becomes available from Reserve, nominate one friendly Summoning Point already on the battlefield.
The following count as Summoning Points:
Personal Icons, Icons of Chaos Undivided, Accursed Crozii, and any other rule specifically stated to act as a Summoning Point.
Place the centre model of the summoned unit within 6" of the Summoning Point and more than 2" from any enemy model. The unit then enters play using the normal Deep Strike rules.
If no eligible Summoning Point or legal position is available, the unit remains in Reserve and must roll for Reserves again during a later turn.
A Summoning Point may be used while its bearer is engaged in close combat and is not consumed when used. The same Summoning Point may summon multiple units during the battle.
Any Deep Strike Mishap is resolved normally.
Units summoned in this manner follow all normal restrictions for units arriving by Deep Strike.
DAEMONOLOGY
Daemonic Covenant is separate from Daemonology (Malefic). Units created through Conjuration psychic powers are not Covenant units and do not use the Daemonic Covenant rules.
THE DARK BRETHREN
FROM BEYOND
A Word Bearers army using The Dark Brethren may form a far deeper pact with the entities of the Warp.
If the army includes a Daemons of the Ruinstorm Covenant Detachment, the following changes apply:
The Covenant may use the normal Daemons of the Ruinstorm Allied Detachment Force Organisation Chart instead of the restricted Covenant chart. The normal 25% points limit is removed. The Detachment instead follows the normal points restrictions for Allied Detachments.
Word Bearers and the Daemons of the Ruinstorm are treated as Sworn Brothers.
Before deployment, each Daemon unit must be designated as either Manifested or Summoned.
Manifested units deploy and enter play normally using the rules from the Daemons of the Ruinstorm Army List.
Summoned units must begin the battle in Reserve and enter play using the Daemonic Summoning rules above.
A Word Bearers army may still include only one Daemons of the Ruinstorm Allied Detachment.
WORD BEARERS ARMOURY
The armouries of the XVII Legion contain an ever-growing collection of occult weapons, blasphemous relics and artefacts touched by the Warp. Many of these objects would once have been destroyed by the Imperial Heralds themselves, but now serve as symbols of the Primordial Truth.
ACCURSED CROZIUS — 40 POINTS
Any Word Bearers Praetor or Centurion may purchase an Accursed Crozius for +40 points. A model equipped with an Accursed Crozius counts as a Dark Apostle for the purposes of The Dark Shepherds.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Accursed Crozius | User | Power Weapon
The bearer receives a 4+ Invulnerable Save and counts as possessing a Personal Icon for the purposes of summoning Daemons.
A model may never possess more than one Accursed Crozius.
TAINTED WEAPON — SAME COST AS A POWER WEAPON
Any Word Bearers Character eligible to select a Power Weapon may instead select a Tainted Weapon for the same points cost.
Weapon | Strength | Special Rules
Tainted Weapon | User | Specialist Weapon, Tainted Strike
TAINTED STRIKE
Any unsaved wound inflicted by a Tainted Weapon becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of 1.
A Tainted Weapon is not a Power Weapon and does not ignore Armour Saves.
BURNING LORE — 30 POINTS
Any Word Bearers Praetor, Centurion, Chaplain or Diabolist which is not already a Psyker may purchase Burning Lore for +30 points.
The model becomes a Psyker with Mastery Level 1 and selects one psychic power from either the Biomancy or Telepathy discipline.
The model follows all normal ProHammer rules for Psykers.
HEX-BOLTS — 5 POINTS PER UNIT
Any Word Bearers Infantry unit equipped with Bolt weapons may purchase Hex-Bolts for +5 points per unit.
Bolt Pistols, Bolters, Combi-Bolters, Storm Bolters and the Bolter component of Combi-Weapons carried by models in the unit gain the Soul Blaze special rule.
Hex-Bolts may not be combined with Special Issue Ammunition or another ammunition upgrade.
ICON OF CHAOS UNDIVIDED — 30 POINTS
One model in a Legion Command Squad, Legion Veteran Squad or Legion Terminator Squad may carry an Icon of Chaos Undivided for +30 points. The Icon counts as a summoning point for the purposes of the Word Bearers' Daemonic Covenant.
In addition, friendly non-Daemon Word Bearers units with at least one model within 6" of the bearer gain the Fearless special rule.
FAVOUR OF THE PANTHEON
One non-named Word Bearers Independent Character in the army may purchase one of the following Favours of the Pantheon. A model may never possess more than one Favour.
Daemonic Aura — 15 points: The model gains a 5+ Invulnerable Save.
Daemonic Mutation — 15 points: The model gains +1 Attack.
Daemonic Strength — 10 points: The model gains +1 Strength.
Daemonic Wings — 20 points: The model becomes Jump Infantry. This may not be combined with a Jump Pack, Bike, Jetbike or Terminator Armour.
Daemonic Visage — 5 points: An enemy unit which loses a close combat involving the bearer suffers an additional -1 Leadership when taking the resulting Morale test.
The effects of a Favour are already included when determining the model's characteristics or special rules and may not be purchased more than once.
WORD BEARERS CONSUL:
DIABOLIST — +35 POINTS
A Word Bearers Centurion may be upgraded to a Diabolist for +35 points.
The Diabolist gains the Daemon and Preferred Enemy (Loyalists) special rules.
A Diabolist may not select a Bike, Jetbike, any form of Terminator Armour, Power Fist or Thunder Hammer.
The presence of at least one Diabolist allows eligible units in the Detachment to purchase Dark Channelling.
A Diabolist remains a Centurion for the purposes of purchasing an Accursed Crozius. A Diabolist equipped with an Accursed Crozius therefore counts as a Dark Apostle for the purposes of The Dark Shepherds.
DARK CHANNELLING — 25 POINTS PER UNIT
If the Detachment includes at least one Diabolist, a Legion Tactical Squad, Legion Veteran Squad, Legion Breacher Siege Squad, Legion Terminator Squad or Legion Assault Squad may purchase Dark Channelling for +25 points per squad.
After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, roll a D6 separately for each unit with Dark Channelling:
1–3 — Zealot: The unit gains the Zealot special rule for the duration of the battle.
4–5 — Unholy Strength: Models in the unit gain +1 Strength for the duration of the battle.
6 — Daemon: The unit gains the Daemon special rule for the duration of the battle. The unit may no longer count as a Scoring Unit. In a mission using Victory Points, the unit also counts as destroyed at the end of the battle even if it survives.
The effects of Dark Channelling apply only to the models which form part of the upgraded squad. Independent Characters or other models which subsequently join the unit do not gain its effects.
WORD BEARERS RITE OF WAR:
THE DARK BRETHREN
Before the corruption of the XVII Legion became manifest, the Word Bearers were renowned for their cohesion and self-sacrifice. After their fall, these same qualities were turned towards darker purposes, entire warbands offering blood and souls to the powers beyond reality in exchange for their favour.
EFFECTS
ARCH-TRAITORS
All Word Bearers Independent Characters in the Detachment gain Preferred Enemy against models belonging to the Loyalist faction.
SIGNS AND PORTENTS
After deployment but before the first turn begins, select one Word Bearers Troops unit and roll a D6.
On a 1–3, all enemy units gain Preferred Enemy against the selected unit for the duration of the battle.
On a 4–6, the selected Word Bearers unit gains Preferred Enemy against all enemy units for the duration of the battle.
FROM BEYOND
A Word Bearers Detachment using this Rite may include an Allied Detachment selected from Codex: Chaos Daemons. This Allied Detachment is treated as Sworn Brothers with the Word Bearers.
This does not prevent the Word Bearers from using their normal Daemonic Covenant rules.
HELL FOLLOWS WITH THEM
Whenever an enemy Psyker suffers a Wound from Perils of the Warp, that Wound becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of 1.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite may only be selected by a Traitor Word Bearers Detachment.
The Detachment must include at least one Diabolist.
The Detachment may include no more than one Heavy Support choice.
The army may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment drawn from another Space Marine Legion.
Any Allied Detachment other than Chaos Daemons is treated as Desperate Allies.
WORD BEARERS RITE OF WAR:
LAST OF THE SERRATED SUN
The Serrated Sun were the first of Lorgar's sons to willingly walk the Path of the Primordial Truth. Their survivors retained the Chapter's mastery of orbital assault warfare, descending upon their enemies alongside the monstrous Gal Vorbak in sudden and overwhelming attacks.
EFFECTS
COMPANY OF MONSTERS
Gal Vorbak Dark Brethren may be selected as Troops choices and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
Every Gal Vorbak unit in the Detachment must purchase either a Legion Drop Pod or Dreadclaw Drop Pod as a Dedicated Transport.
DROP ELITE
Any Word Bearers Infantry unit which may normally purchase a Rhino as a Dedicated Transport may instead purchase a Legion Drop Pod at its normal points cost.
BURNING SUN
Whenever a Legion Drop Pod or Dreadclaw Drop Pod belonging to this Detachment arrives using Deep Strike, every enemy unit with at least one model within 12" of the vehicle's final position must immediately take a Pinning test.
A unit need only take one Pinning test for each arriving Drop Pod, regardless of how many of its models are within 12".
LIMITATIONS
This Rite may only be selected by a Traitor Word Bearers Detachment.
All Infantry units in the Detachment must begin the battle in Reserve and enter play using a Deep Striking Drop Pod, Teleportation Transponders or embarked aboard a Transport with the Flyer type.
The army may not include Immobile units.
The army may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XVIII Legion — Salamanders" id="legion-xviii" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xviii-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Salamanders)" id="legion-xviii-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Salamanders. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Salamanders). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Salamanders — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xviii-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
PROMETHEAN CULT
The Salamanders possess an unrivalled mastery of flame, melta weaponry and the weapons of the forge.
Salamanders models may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when attacking with:
• Thunder Hammers
• Melta Bombs
• Meltaguns
• Multi-Meltas
• other weapons with the Melta special rule
In addition, Salamanders models may re-roll To Wound rolls of 1 when firing Flame weapons.
STURDY
The warriors of Nocturne are exceptionally strong and powerfully built, but lack some of the speed of their brother Legions.
All Salamanders models with an Initiative characteristic, except Dreadnoughts, suffer -1 Initiative.
This modifier applies after all other profile modifications. Salamanders units also subtract 1" from their Fall Back distance, to a minimum of 1".
The Initiative penalty applies normally when resolving Pursuit.
NEVER GIVE UP
The Salamanders possess a legendary refusal to accept defeat.
At the end of the final scheduled game turn, the Salamanders player may choose to play one additional complete game turn.
Both players take one additional turn.
After this additional game turn has been completed, the battle ends automatically.
This rule may only be used once per battle and does not extend a mission which has already ended because a specific objective or action was completed.
SALAMANDERS ARMOURY
The warriors of Nocturne are craftsmen as much as soldiers, each Legionary taught to maintain and improve his own equipment. The greatest artificers of the XVIII Legion produce weapons and armour of exceptional quality, particularly those intended to withstand or unleash the fury of flame.
SALAMANDERS MANTLE — 35 POINTS
One Salamanders Independent Character in the army may purchase a Salamanders Mantle for +35 points.
If an unsaved Wound would become a Massive Wound solely because the attack's Strength is at least double the bearer's Toughness, it instead inflicts only one Wound.
The Mantle provides no protection against weapons or special rules which explicitly inflict Massive Wounds by another method.
Only one Salamanders Mantle may be included in the army. A named Character whose entry already includes a Salamanders Mantle prevents another model from purchasing one.
ARTIFICER WEAPONS
Salamanders models purchase the Master-crafted Weapon upgrade for +10 points rather than the normal +15 points.
All normal restrictions on Master-crafted Weapons continue to apply.
ARTIFICER ARMOUR
A Salamanders non-Independent Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase Artificer Armour for +15 points even if his unit entry would not normally allow him to do so.
If the model's own unit entry already offers Artificer Armour at a lower points cost, use the cost listed in that unit entry instead.
FIRE-BASED WARFARE
Flamers and Heavy Flamers used by Salamanders models gain +1 Strength. They May be referred to as Dragons Breath flamer
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Flamer | Template | 5 | 5 | Assault 1
Heavy Flamer | Template | 6 | 4 | Assault 1
Where a Legion Tactical Squad or Legion Veteran Squad may purchase a Flamer, it may instead purchase a Heavy Flamer for +10 points.
Legion Heavy Support Squads may select Heavy Flamers as a Heavy Weapon option for +10 points per model.
INFERNO PISTOL — 15 POINTS
Any Salamanders Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase an Inferno Pistol for +15 points.
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Inferno Pistol | 6" | 8 | 1 | Pistol, Melta
REINFORCED CERAMITE
Any Salamanders Vehicle or Dreadnought which may normally purchase Armoured Ceramite may purchase it for +10 points instead of its normal points cost.
Land Raiders and Spartans purchase Armoured Ceramite at their normal listed cost.
The upgrade otherwise follows the normal Armoured Ceramite rules.
PROSCRIBED MUNITIONS
A Salamanders Detachment may not select Phosphex weapons or Phosphex ammunition unless a specific unit or Character entry explicitly states otherwise.
SALAMANDERS RITE OF WAR:
THE COVENANT OF FIRE
The Covenant of Fire represents the characteristic method of war taught by Vulkan: an inexorable advance through the enemy's strongest resistance, protected by master-crafted armour and supported by overwhelming flame and melta weaponry.
EFFECTS
DISCIPLES OF THE FLAME
Pyroclast Squads and Salamanders Infernus Destroyer Squads may be selected as non-compulsory Troops choices.
They may not fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
WALK THROUGH FIRE
Salamanders Infantry units gain the Move Through Cover special rule.
VENERATION OF WRATH
When a Salamanders model makes an Armour Penetration roll with a Melta weapon, one individual Armour Penetration die which rolls a natural 1 may be re-rolled. The second result must be accepted.
This also applies to Melta Bombs.
OBSIDIAN FORGED
Each time a Salamanders Vehicle or Dreadnought suffers a Glancing or Penetrating Hit from an attack made with a Flame,
Melta, Plasma or Volkite weapon, roll a D6. On a 5+, the hit is ignored. Make this roll before rolling on the Vehicle Damage table.
This protection also applies against Glancing or Penetrating Hits caused by Melta Bombs.
LIMITATIONS
Units in the Detachment may not deploy using Deep Strike. Units which must deploy using Deep Strike may not be selected.
The combined number of Fast Attack and Heavy Support choices may not exceed the number of Troops choices in the Detachment.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
SALAMANDERS RITE OF WAR:
THE AWAKENING FIRE
After Vulkan was lost upon Isstvan V, some among the XVIII Legion turned ever deeper towards the mysteries of the Promethean Cult. Their grief became a terrible certainty, and the sons of Nocturne began to appear to their enemies as creatures born from the flames themselves.
EFFECTS
DEVILS FROM THE DARK
Salamanders Infantry units gain the Fear special rule.
UNTO THE FIRES
Never Give Up functions normally.
During the additional complete game turn generated by Never Give Up, all Salamanders Infantry units gain the Fearless special rule.
FURY OF THE SALAMANDER
Salamanders Librarians in the Detachment may select Fury of the Salamander as a Pyromancy psychic power.
Psychic Power | Range | Strength | AP | Type
Fury of the Salamander | 18" | 5 | 1 | Witchfire — Beam, Assault 1, Elemental Horror
ELEMENTAL HORROR
If an enemy unit suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from Fury of the Salamander, it must immediately take a Morale test regardless of how many casualties were caused.
The unit suffers a Leadership penalty to this test equal to the number of unsaved Wounds caused by Fury of the Salamander.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must include a Legion Chaplain Consul.
The Detachment may include no more than one unit of each of the following types: Jump Infantry, Jetbike, Skimmer and Flyer.
The Detachment may not include Vulkan.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XIX Legion — Raven Guard" id="legion-xix" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xix-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard)" id="legion-xix-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Raven Guard. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Raven Guard — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xix-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
SURGICAL STRIKE
The Raven Guard specialise in sudden attacks upon carefully identified weak points in the enemy line.
Whenever a Raven Guard unit deploys using Deep Strike, the Raven Guard player may re-roll the Scatter die and any dice rolled for scatter distance. The entire result must be re-rolled and the second result must be accepted.
RAPID REACTION
Raven Guard reconnaissance elements act as the eyes of the Legion, directing incoming reserves towards precisely identified points of weakness.
At the beginning of each Raven Guard turn, if at least one friendly Legion Reconnaissance Squad or Mor Deythan Squad has a surviving model on the battlefield and is not Falling Back, add +1 to all Raven Guard Reserve rolls made during that turn.
This bonus is not cumulative.
SHADOW MASTERS
Reconnaissance formations form an integral part of Raven Guard battle doctrine rather than merely supporting the main Legion line.
Legion Reconnaissance Squads selected in a Raven Guard Detachment lose the Support Squad special rule.
They may therefore fulfil compulsory Troops selections normally. Legion Reconnaissance Squads and Independent Characters may buy Sniper Rifles for 2 points instead of 5points or any price otherwise applicable.
LIMITED VEHICLES
The Raven Guard favour mobility and stealth over the massed deployment of heavy armour.
A Raven Guard Detachment may never include more Heavy Support selections than Fast Attack selections.
Dedicated Transports are ignored when determining this restriction.
RAVEN GUARD ARMOURY
The XIX Legion favours equipment suited to reconnaissance, infiltration and sudden violence at close range. Much of its specialist wargear derives from the technologies of Kiavahr and the traditions of the freedom fighters of Deliverance.
RAVEN’S TALONS — 7 POINTS PER MODEL
Any model in a Raven Guard Legion Veteran Squad equipped with a Bolt pistol and Chainsword may replace both weapons with a
pair of Raven's Talons for +7 points. A Raven Guard Character already equipped with a pair of
Lightning Claws may upgrade them to Raven's Talons for +5 points. Raven's Talons count as a pair of Rending Weapons.
The bearer therefore receives the normal +1 Attack bonus for fighting with two close-combat weapons.
Other units may only select Raven's Talons where specificallypermitted by their unit entry.
FULCRUM HAND CANNON — 10 POINTS
Any Raven Guard Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may replace a Bolt Pistol with a Fulcrum Hand Cannon for +10 points.
A Raven Guard Moritat may replace either or both of his Bolt Pistols with Fulcrum Hand Cannons for +10 points each.
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Fulcrum Hand Cannon | 18" | 4 | 4 | Pistol, Rending, Concussive
INFRAVISOR — 10 POINTS
Any Raven Guard Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase an Infravisor for +10 points.
The bearer gains the Night Vision special rule and +1 Ballistic Skill, to a maximum of BS6.
When taking an Initiative test caused by the Blind special rule, the bearer and any unit he has joined count as Initiative 1.
SHROUD BOMBS — 10/20 POINTS
A Raven Guard Independent Character may purchase Shroud Bombs for +10 points. A Legion Reconnaissance Squad, Legion Veteran Squad or Mor Deythan Squad may purchase Shroud Bombs for +20 points per squad.
Shroud Bombs count as Defensive Grenades.
In addition, an enemy unit attempting to charge a unit equipped with Shroud Bombs must first pass a Leadership test. If the test is failed, the charge may not be attempted and the enemy unit may not declare another charge that turn.
Vehicles, models with the Daemon special rule and units containing a model with Night Vision are unaffected by this rule.
CAMELEOLINE
Raven Guard Legion Reconnaissance Squads retain their normal option to purchase Cameleoline from their unit entry.
A Raven Guard Independent Character wearing Power Armour, Artificer Armour or Recon Armour may purchase Cameleoline for +10 points.
Cameleoline grants the Stealth special rule.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Raven Guard unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit. A Raven Guard Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase them for +10 points.
A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders gains the Deep Strike special rule and may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit it.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
RAVEN GUARD RITE OF WAR:
DECAPITATION STRIKE
The Raven Guard do not seek victory through attrition when a single precisely delivered blow will suffice. Commanders, communications centres and strategic assets are identified, isolated and destroyed before the enemy can bring its full strength to bear.
EFFECTS
FOR WHOM THE BELL TOLLS
All Raven Guard units gain Preferred Enemy (Independent Characters).
For the purposes of this rule, an enemy unit containing one or more Independent Characters counts as a Preferred Enemy until all Independent Characters in that unit have either been slain or left the unit.
PREDATORY STRIKE
If the mission requires a roll to determine deployment order, choice of deployment zone or which player takes the first turn, the Raven Guard player may re-roll that roll. The entire result must be re-rolled and the second result must be accepted.
This ability may only be used once per battle.
FURY FROM ABOVE
Raven Guard Legion Heavy Support Squads must select either a Legion Drop Pod or Anvillus Dreadclaw Drop Pod as a Dedicated Transport at its normal points cost. All normal Transport Capacity and deployment restrictions apply.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment may include no more than one Heavy Support choice.
The Detachment may include no more than one Centurion upgraded to a Consul.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment drawn from another Space Marine Legion.
RAVEN GUARD RITE OF WAR:
LIBERATION FORCE
After the massacre at Isstvan V, Corax and the surviving Raven Guard turned their strength towards worlds oppressed by the Warmaster. These forces combined the Legion’s mastery of asymmetric warfare with local armies inspired by the example of the XIX Legion.
EFFECTS
FREEDOM FIGHTERS
Once per battle, at the beginning of any Game Turn, the Raven Guard player may declare Freedom Fighters.
Until the end of that Game Turn, every model in the Raven Guard Detachment and any allied Imperialis Militia Detachment gains the Zealot special rule.
SLAYERS OF TYRANTS
If the mission awards Victory Points for slaying the enemy Warlord, replace the normal Victory Point award with D3 times its normal value.
For example, if the mission normally awards 50 Victory Points for slaying the enemy Warlord, this Rite awards D3 × 50 Victory Points instead.
LEAD BY EXAMPLE
Models belonging to an allied Imperialis Militia Detachment gain the Fearless special rule while they have at least one model within 6" of a friendly model with Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard).
LIBERATORS
An Allied Detachment drawn from the Imperialis Militia may be included without preventing the use of this Rite of War.
All other normal rules governing Allied Detachments continue to apply.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Loyalist Raven Guard Detachment.
The Detachment may not include units with the Immobile or Slow and Purposeful special rules.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="XX Legion — Alpha Legion" id="legion-xx" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="legion-xx-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)" id="legion-xx-named" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Detachment is Alpha Legion. Models with the Legiones Astartes special rule gain Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion). Legion-specific rules, units, wargear and characters are unlocked by this selection where applicable.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Alpha Legion — Legion Rules &amp; Armoury" id="r25-legion-xx-reference" hidden="false">
                  <description>LEGION SPECIAL RULES
MUTABLE TACTICS
An Alpha Legion army must select one of the following Veteran Skills at the point where Warlord Traits are selected for the game. This rule applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units in the detachment with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) for the duration of the game. This does not count towards the number of Veteran Skills a unit may have. All normal restrictions associated with the selected Veteran Skill continue to apply.
• Counter-Attack
• Furious Charge
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Siege Specialists
• Tank Hunters
SIEGE SPECIALISTS
A unit using Siege Specialists receives +1 to Armour Penetration rolls against Fortifications, Buildings, Bunkers and other immobile structures with an Armour Value. All other abilities use their normal ProHammer rules.
MARTIAL HUBRIS
The Alpha Legion deliberately seeks complex victories intended to demonstrate its superiority, even when a simpler plan would be more efficient.
In a mission using Victory Points, compare the number of completely destroyed units belonging to each player at the end of the battle.
If more Alpha Legion units have been completely destroyed than enemy units, the opposing player receives an additional D3 x 50 Victory Points.
If both players have lost the same number of units, this rule has no effect.
INFILTRATION NETWORK
Alpha Legion operations are routinely prepared by infiltrators, agents and mortal operatives long before the Legion openly enters battle.
Legion Operative units may be selected as Troops choices in an Alpha Legion Detachment.
Up to two Legion Operative units may be selected without occupying a Troops selection on the Force Organisation Chart.
These units must still be paid for normally and count as units for the purposes of Martial Hubris.
ALPHA LEGION ARMOURY
The XX Legion maintained arsenals suited to infiltration, sabotage and targeted assassination. Much of its specialist equipment was designed not for open battle, but to ensure that when the Alpha Legion finally revealed its hand, the enemy was already compromised.
BANESTRIKE AMMUNITION — 5 POINTS PER MODEL
Alpha Legion Seeker Squads, Legion Veteran Squads and Independent Characters equipped with a Bolter, Foeblaster Boltgun, Combi-Bolter or Combi-Weapon may purchase Banestrike Ammunition for +5 points per eligible model. Every eligible model in a squad must purchase the upgrade or none may do so. When firing Banestrike Ammunition, use the Banestrike profile presented below.
When used with a Foeblaster Boltgun, Combi-Bolter or the Bolter component of a Combi-Weapon, retain the weapon's normal number of shots and firing type but reduce its range to 18", use AP4 and apply the Banestrike special rule.
Seeker Squads retain their normal Special Issue Ammunition and may choose to fire Banestrike Ammunition instead whenever they shoot.
Banestrike Ammunition may not be combined with another ammunition type.
Weapon | Range | Strength | AP | Special Rules
Banestrike Bolter | 18" | 4 | 4 | Rapid Fire, Banestrike
BANESTRIKE
A natural To Wound roll of 6 made with Banestrike Ammunition is resolved at AP3.
POWER DAGGER — 5 POINTS
Any Alpha Legion Character with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase a Power Dagger for +5 points.
A Power Dagger counts as a Power Weapon with the Rending and Specialist Weapon special rules.
Attacks made with a Power Dagger are resolved at -1 Strength.
VENOM SPHERES — 5 POINTS
Any Alpha Legion Independent Character or squad Sergeant with access to the Space Marine Armoury may purchase Venom Spheres for +5 points. The bearer gains the Hammer of Wrath special rule. Units specifically permitted to purchase Venom Spheres in their own army list entry use the points cost given there instead.
LEGION SABOTEUR — +25 POINTS
One Alpha Legion Seeker Sergeant in the army may be upgraded to a Legion Saboteur for +25 points.
The Saboteur retains the profile, weapons and equipment of the model he replaces.
COORDINATED SABOTAGE
After Mutable Tactics has been selected, the Saboteur's squad may select one additional Veteran Skill from the Mutable Tactics list at no additional points cost.
A skill already granted by Mutable Tactics may not be selected again.
PRE-EMPTIVE STRIKE
After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, nominate one enemy unit.
If a non-Vehicle unit is selected, it suffers D6 Strength 4 hits. Armour Saves may be taken normally. If at least one casualty is caused, the unit must immediately take a Pinning test with a -1 Leadership modifier.
If a Vehicle is selected, roll a D6. On a 1–3 there is no effect. On a 4–5 the Vehicle suffers one Glancing Hit. On a 6 it suffers one Penetrating Hit.
A Pre-emptive Strike requires no range or line of sight.
TELEPORTATION TRANSPONDERS
Any Alpha Legion unit composed entirely of models wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase Teleportation Transponders for +15 points per unit. An Alpha Legion Independent Character wearing any form of Terminator Armour may purchase them for +10 points.
A model or unit equipped with Teleportation Transponders gains the Deep Strike special rule and may deploy using Deep Strike even if the mission would not normally permit it.
An Independent Character intending to Deep Strike as part of another unit must purchase Teleportation Transponders separately.
ALPHA LEGION RITE OF WAR:
THE COILS OF THE HYDRA
The Alpha Legion rarely wages war according to a single plan. False deployments, corrupted communications, infiltrated enemy formations and concealed reserves form overlapping layers of deception until the foe can no longer distinguish the true attack from the feint.
EFFECTS
SUBTERFUGE
Before determining which player takes the first turn, the Alpha Legion player must choose one of the following benefits: add +1 to their roll to determine who takes the first turn, or re-roll a failed attempt to Seize the Initiative.
The choice must be made before any relevant dice are rolled.
SIGNAL CORRUPTION
Enemy Reserve rolls suffer a -1 modifier.
This modifier applies to normal Reserve rolls but does not affect units which enter play automatically on a specified turn.
THE REWARDS OF TREACHERY
The Detachment may include one Legion-specific unit normally available only to another Space Marine Legion.
The selected unit may not be a Primarch, named Character, Independent Character or a unit specifically marked as Unique.
The unit is selected as an Elites choice and is paid for normally. It retains its normal profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific version of Legiones Astartes with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion).
The unit therefore benefits from the Alpha Legion's rules, including Mutable Tactics, but does not benefit from the core Legion rules of its original Legion.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must take one additional compulsory Troops choice, for a total of three compulsory Troops choices.
Every Infantry unit in the Detachment must possess Infiltrate or Deep Strike, or must have access to and purchase a Dedicated Transport.
If an Infantry unit relies upon Mutable Tactics to satisfy this requirement, Infiltrate must be selected as the army's Mutable Tactic for that battle.
The Detachment may include no more than one Centurion upgraded to a Consul, although Vigilator Consuls do not count towards this restriction.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment drawn from another Space Marine Legion.
ALPHA LEGION RITE OF WAR:
HEADHUNTER LEVIATHAL
The elite Headhunter cadres of the XX Legion were employed to remove commanders, communications officers and other strategically vital individuals before the enemy understood that a battle had even begun.
EFFECTS
HEADHUNTER ELITE
Headhunter Kill Teams may be selected as Troops choices and must be used to fulfil the Detachment's compulsory Troops selections.
Additional Headhunter Kill Teams may also be selected as Troops choices.
SUDDEN STRIKE
The Alpha Legion player may re-roll the dice used to determine which player takes the first turn.
The entire result must be re-rolled and the second result must be accepted.
FALSE FLAGS
During the first Game Turn, an enemy unit which declares a shooting attack against an Alpha Legion unit must first pass a Leadership test unless that enemy unit has already been fired upon by an Alpha Legion unit during the current player turn.
If the test is passed, the shooting attack is resolved normally. If the test is failed, the unit may not make that shooting attack.
False Flags does not affect Overwatch, Return Fire or Stand &amp; Shoot attacks.
LEAVE NO HEAD UPON THE SERPENT
The Alpha Legion must destroy the enemy Warlord before the end of the battle.
If the enemy Warlord survives, the opposing player gains an additional D3 × 50 Victory Points.
This rule has no effect in missions which do not use Victory Points.
LIMITATIONS
Every Alpha Legion Vehicle must begin the battle in Reserve unless a mission specifically prohibits it from doing so.
The Detachment may not include an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <selectionEntryGroups>
                <selectionEntryGroup id="r46-al-mutable-tactics" name="Mutable Tactics" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
                  <constraints>
                    <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-min" type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </constraints>
                  <selectionEntries>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-0" name="Counter-Attack" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
                        <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-0-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </constraints>
                      <rules>
                        <rule id="r46-al-mutable-0-rule" name="Counter-Attack" hidden="false">
                          <description>Selected as the Alpha Legion army’s Mutable Tactic. Applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units and does not count toward their Veteran Skill limit. Normal restrictions of the selected skill apply.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
                    </selectionEntry>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-1" name="Furious Charge" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
                        <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-1-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </constraints>
                      <rules>
                        <rule id="r46-al-mutable-1-rule" name="Furious Charge" hidden="false">
                          <description>Selected as the Alpha Legion army’s Mutable Tactic. Applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units and does not count toward their Veteran Skill limit. Normal restrictions of the selected skill apply.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
                    </selectionEntry>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-2" name="Infiltrate" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
                        <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-2-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </constraints>
                      <rules>
                        <rule id="r46-al-mutable-2-rule" name="Infiltrate" hidden="false">
                          <description>Selected as the Alpha Legion army’s Mutable Tactic. Applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units and does not count toward their Veteran Skill limit. Normal restrictions of the selected skill apply.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
                    </selectionEntry>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-3" name="Move Through Cover" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
                        <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-3-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </constraints>
                      <rules>
                        <rule id="r46-al-mutable-3-rule" name="Move Through Cover" hidden="false">
                          <description>Selected as the Alpha Legion army’s Mutable Tactic. Applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units and does not count toward their Veteran Skill limit. Normal restrictions of the selected skill apply.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
                    </selectionEntry>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-4" name="Siege Specialists" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
                        <constraint id="r46-al-mutable-4-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </constraints>
                      <rules>
                        <rule id="r46-al-mutable-4-rule" name="Siege Specialists" hidden="false">
                          <description>Selected as the Alpha Legion army’s Mutable Tactic. Applies to all qualifying non-vehicle units and does not count toward their Veteran Skill limit. Normal restrictions of the selected skill apply.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
                    </selectionEntry>
                    <selectionEntry id="r46-al-mutable-5" name="Tank Hunters" type="upgrade" hidden="false" import="true">
                      <constraints>
