        </rule>
        <rule name="Super-heavy Tank Shock" id="r32-low-falchion-low-3" hidden="false">
          <description>A Super-heavy Vehicle with the Tank unit type may Tank Shock and Ram using the normal ProHammer rules. Enemy units taking a Tank Shock Test caused by it suffer -1 Leadership.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Crushing Advance" id="r32-low-falchion-low-4" hidden="false">
          <description>Super-heavy Vehicles ignore low walls, hedges, rubble, barricades and similarly minor obstacles. Other Difficult Terrain is Dangerous Terrain as normal. A failed Dangerous Terrain test causes an Engine Damaged result instead of Immobilised.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Immense Machine" id="r32-low-falchion-low-5" hidden="false">
          <description>Crew Shaken: the attacker chooses one weapon; that weapon may only fire Snap Shots until the end of the vehicle's next turn. Crew Stunned: the vehicle may not move in its next Movement phase and the attacker chooses one weapon that may only fire Snap Shots until the end of the vehicle's next turn; all other weapons may fire normally. Other damage results are resolved normally, including Structure Points.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Catastrophic Destruction" id="r32-low-falchion-low-6" hidden="false">
          <description>When finally destroyed after reaching 0 Structure Points, roll a D6. 1-3: Wrecked. 4-5: Explosion; models within D6" suffer S5 AP- and vehicles are hit at S5 against Side Armour. 6: Catastrophic Explosion; roll one D3 per starting Structure Point and total the result for the radius in inches; models suffer S6 AP- and vehicles are hit at S6 against Side Armour.</description>
        </rule>
