    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XIV — MORTARION, THE REAPER" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-8-xiv-mortarion-the-reaper">
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="500" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiv-8-xiv-mortarion-the-reaper-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" primary="true" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiv" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="r41-unit-xiv-8-xiv-mortarion-the-reaper-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mortarion" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-8-xiv-mortarion-the-reaper-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiv-8-xiv-mortarion-the-reaper-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Primarch of the Death Guard, the Pale King, the Reaper of Men
Mortarion was raised beneath the poisoned skies of Barbarus, a world where survival itself was a war against toxic atmosphere, monstrous overlords and the slow certainty of death. From those beginnings came a Primarch of almost inexhaustible endurance, possessed of a hatred for tyranny, witchcraft and weakness in all their forms. Where others sought brilliance of manoeuvre or the glory of the decisive charge, Mortarion believed that victory belonged to the warrior who simply refused to die.
Under his command the XIV Legion became the Death Guard, an army fashioned in its Primarch's image. They advanced through irradiated wastelands, chemical storms and burning ruins with the same remorseless pace, grinding their enemies beneath relentless fire and brutal close assault. Mortarion himself strode at the centre of such offensives, wreathed in poisonous vapours and bearing the immense battle-scythe Silence, a spectral figure whose coming promised only death. This identity is also strongly reflected in the existing Death Guard rules, which already emphasise poison resistance and infantry advancing through hostile terrain.
Mortarion | 7 | 6 | 6 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Mortarion
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Barbaran Plate
• Silence
• Lantern
• Phosphex Bomb
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Death Guard)
• Barbaran Endurance
• Witch-Spite
• Toxic Miasma
• Poison Cannot Kill Death
BARBARAN PLATE Forged to withstand conditions which would prove lethal even to a Space Marine, Barbaran Plate incorporated extensive environmental sealing and protection against chemical, biological and radiological attack. Barbaran Plate counts as Primarch Armour. SILENCE An immense battle-scythe fashioned to the proportions of the Death Guard Primarch, Silence was a weapon whose sweeping blows could reap whole ranks of warriors and cut apart the mightiest champions of the Great Crusade. Silence is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with Silence are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Rampage special rule. Any unsaved Wound inflicted by Silence against a model without the Primarch special rule becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of one Wound. LANTERN A rare and immensely powerful Shenlongi energy weapon, Lantern was capable of punching through armour and war machines with concentrated blasts of incandescent energy. Weapon Range S AP Type Lantern 18" 8 2 Assault 1, Armourbane, Master-crafted PHOSPHEX BOMB Mortarion carried amongst his arsenal weapons filled with the nightmare substance known as phosphex, a proscribed incendiary compound infamous for pursuing living prey and rendering the ground itself lethal. Weapon Range S AP Type Phosphex Bomb 6" 5 2 Assault 1, Blast, One Use, Poisoned (3+), Lingering Death The Phosphex Bomb follows the normal rules for Phosphex Bombs and Lingering Death presented in the Legiones Astartes Army List. BARBARAN ENDURANCE Few beings in the Imperium could match Mortarion's ability to endure injury, exhaustion and environments capable of killing lesser warriors in moments. Mortarion has Feel No Pain (5+). WITCH-SPITE Mortarion possessed a deep and abiding hatred of sorcery, born during his enslavement beneath the witch-lords of Barbarus and strengthened by his distrust of those who wielded the powers of the Warp. Whenever Mortarion or a unit he has joined makes a Deny the Witch roll, a failed roll may be re-rolled. In addition, Mortarion's Adamantium Will grants a +2 bonus to Deny the Witch rolls instead of the normal +1. THE REAPER\`S ADVANCE Friendly Death Guard Infantry within 12" of Mortarion may fire Rapid Fire weapons as though they had remained stationary. In addition, they may re-roll failed Pinning tests. TOXIC MIASMA The armour and wargear of the Death Lord surrounded him with a haze of poisonous vapours and corrosive contaminants, lethal to any foe forced to fight at close quarters. Enemy non-Vehicle models in base contact with Mortarion suffer -1 Toughness. This penalty lasts only while the model remains in base contact with Mortarion. POISON CANNOT KILL DEATH The poisons which slew armies and the polluted atmosphere of Barbarus itself had shaped Mortarion into a being all but impossible to kill through toxin or contagion. Poisoned attacks made against Mortarion do not use their normal fixed To Wound value. Instead, resolve the attack using its Strength against Mortarion's Toughness normally. If a Poisoned attack has no Strength characteristic, it may only wound Mortarion on an unmodified roll of 6. PRIMARCH RETINUE Mortarion may select one Deathshroud Terminator Squad as his Primarch Retinue. Mortarion may not select a Legion Honour Guard Squad or Legion Terminator Command Squad as his Primarch Retinue. A Deathshroud Terminator Squad selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="MORTARION, PRINCE OF DECAY" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-9-mortarion-prince-of-decay">
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="650" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiv-9-mortarion-prince-of-decay-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" primary="true" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiv" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="r41-unit-xiv-9-mortarion-prince-of-decay-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mortarion, Prince of Decay" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-9-mortarion-prince-of-decay-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4++</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiv-9-mortarion-prince-of-decay-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Daemon Primarch of Nurgle
Mortarion endured a transformation he had once despised above all things. His body swollen with corruption and borne upon vast ragged wings, the Death Lord became a living vessel of pestilence. Where Mortarion walks, flesh rots, armour corrodes and the air itself becomes poison. Unlike his brothers, the Daemon Primarch does not descend upon his enemies in glorious flight or frenzied fury. He simply advances, inexorable and enduring, until everything around him begins to die.
Mortarion, Prince of Decay | 7 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 8 | 4 | 5 | 10 | 2+/4++
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Mortarion, Prince of Decay
Unit Type:
• Monstrous Creature (Character)
Wargear:
• Silence
• Lantern
• Daemonic Barbaran Plate
Special Rules:
• Daemon
• Fear
• Fearless
• Eternal Warrior
• Feel No Pain (5+)
• Poison Resistance
• Adamantium Will
• Master of the Legion
• Psyker (Mastery Level 2\)
• Burdened Wings
• The Reaper’s Miasma
• Reluctant Sorcerer
• Sons of the Plague Father
RESTRICTIONS
Mortarion, Prince of Decay may only be selected for a Death Guard army. An army may not include both Mortarion, Prince of Decay and Mortarion in his mortal form.
BURDENED WINGS Mortarion may move over intervening models and terrain as though using a Jump Pack, but may never move more than 9" during the Movement phase. Mortarion may never join another unit and no model may join him. SILENCE Silence is a Two-Handed, Master-crafted Power Weapon which grants Mortarion +2 Strength. Instead of making his normal close-combat attacks, Mortarion may make one attack against every enemy model in base contact with him. LANTERN Weapon Range S AP Type Lantern 18" 8 2 Assault 1, Master-crafted THE REAPER’S MIASMA At the beginning of each enemy turn, every enemy unit within 18" of Mortarion suffers the appropriate effect: Distance Effect Within 6" D3 S5 AP4 hits, Poisoned (3+) 6–12" D3 S4 AP4 hits, Poisoned (3+) 12–18" 1 S4 AP4 hit, Poisoned (3+) Death Guard models and Daemons of Nurgle are immune. RELUCTANT SORCERER Mortarion is a Mastery Level 2 Psyker, but always takes Psychic Tests using Leadership 8, regardless of his normal Leadership or modifiers which would increase it. Mortarion knows the following powers: MIASMA OF PESTILENCE Phase: Beginning of the enemy Assault phase
Range: 12" Choose one enemy unit within range and take a Psychic Test. If successful, the unit suffers –1 Initiative and –1 Attack, to a minimum of 1, until the end of the Assault phase. CURSE OF DECAY Phase: Mortarion’s Shooting phase
Range: 18" Choose one enemy unit within range and take a Psychic Test. If successful, the unit treats all terrain, including open ground, as Difficult Terrain until the beginning of Mortarion’s next turn. NURGLE’S ROT Phase: Mortarion’s Shooting phase
Range: 12" Choose one enemy unit within range and take a Psychic Test. If successful, the target suffers D6 Strength 4 AP4 hits with Poisoned (3+). SONS OF THE PLAGUE FATHER If Daemon Primarch Mortarion is included in a Death Guard army, a Death Guard Infantry unit composed entirely of models wearing Power Armour or Artificer Armour may be upgraded to Plague Marines for: +7 points per model Models upgraded in this manner gain: • +1 Toughness
• Feel No Pain (5+)
• Slow and Purposeful Models upgraded to Plague Marines may not benefit from Move Through Cover, regardless of its source. Their normal maximum charge distance is reduced from 6" to 5", and they may not benefit from rules which increase their Movement or charge distance. The Relentless component of Slow and Purposeful applies normally. |</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
