    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="NUMEROLOGIST CABAL" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xv-5-numerologist-cabal">
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="55.0" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="r41-unit-xv-5-numerologist-cabal-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" primary="true" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xv" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Numerologist" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xv-5-numerologist-cabal-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Life Ward" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xv-5-numerologist-cabal-profile-1">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xv-5-numerologist-cabal-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Numerologist | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+
Life Ward | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 8 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
ORDER OF RUIN When the army is selected, assign the Numerologist Cabal to one Prosperine Cult normally. The Cabal receives the Cult Arcana of that Cult. While the Numerologist remains alive, it also receives Cult's Cult Mastery benefit. The Numerologist knows only Psy-Synchronicity. PSY-SYNCHRONICITY Psy-Synchronicity is a Blessing invoked during the Thousand Sons Movement phase. If successfully invoked, select up to two friendly Thousand Sons units with at least one model within 6" of the Numerologist. Until the end of the following Thousand Sons Shooting phase, models in those units may re-roll shooting To Hit rolls of 1. The Numerologist may not fire a weapon during a player turn in which he successfully invokes Psy-Synchronicity. BATTLESMITH The Numerologist uses the normal Battlesmith rule.His Servo-Arm grants the normal +1 bonus to repair attempts.
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 1 Numerologist
• 4 Life Wards
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Numerologist is a Character
Wargear — Numerologist:
• Artificer Armour
• Bolt pistol
• Chainsword
• Servo-Arm
• Frag grenades
Wargear — Life Wards:
• Power Armour
• Bolt pistol
• Chainsword
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)
• Psyker (Mastery Level 1\) — Numerologist only
• Battlesmith — Numerologist only
• Order of Ruin
OPTIONS
• The Cabal may include up to five additional Life Wards for +15 points per model.
• The Numerologist may replace his Chainsword with:
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Prosperine Force Weapon ..................... +20 points
• Thunder hammer .............................. +20 points
• The Numerologist may replace his Bolt pistol with:
• Volkite Charger ............................... +5 points
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Plasma Gun ................................... +15 points
• Meltagun ..................................... +15 points
• Graviton Gun ................................. +15 points
• For every five models in the Cabal, one Life Ward may replace
his Bolt pistol with:
• Rotor Cannon .................................. +5 points
• Volkite Caliver .............................. +10 points
• One Life Ward may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ............................... +10 points
• One other Life Ward may carry:
