      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Primarch of the Sons of Horus, Warmaster, Vessel of the Four
At the height of the Siege of Terra, Horus Lupercal had become something greater and more terrible than even a Primarch. Empowered by all four Gods of Chaos, the Warmaster stood as the supreme champion of the Traitor host, possessed of unnatural strength, resilience and speed while the powers of the Warp themselves bent to his will.
Horus Ascended | 9 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Horus Ascended
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Serpent's Scales
• Worldbreaker
• The Talon of Horus
• Frag Grenades
• Krak Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Will of the Warmaster
• Master of the Speartip
• The First Company
• The Vengeful Spirit
• Vessel of the Four
• Favoured of the Dark Gods
• Blessings of the Four
• The Warmaster Must Lead
SERPENT'S SCALES The Serpent's Scales confer Horus a 1+ Armour Save and 3+ Invulnerable Save. WORLDBREAKER Worldbreaker is a Master-crafted Thunder Hammer. Horus strikes with Worldbreaker at Initiative 4 rather than Initiative 1. All other Thunder Hammer rules apply normally. THE TALON OF HORUS The Talon counts as a Master-crafted Lightning Claw and grants +1 Strength. It incorporates a Twin-linked Storm Bolter which may use any ammunition from his previous Entry Horus may divide his Attacks between Worldbreaker and the Talon of Horus in any combination. WILL OF THE WARMASTER Friendly Sons of Horus units with line of sight to Horus may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests. Friendly Sons of Horus units with at least one model within 12" of Horus are Fearless. MASTER OF THE SPEARTIP When Horus commands the army, one additional eligible Sons of Horus Elite unit may use the Legion's Tip of the Spear deployment rule. THE FIRST COMPANY Horus may take a Justaerin Terminator Squad as his retinue instead of a normal Command Squad or Terminator Command Squad. Legion Terminators and Justaerin also receive any additional availability granted by the Sons of Horus army list while Horus is present. THE VENGEFUL SPIRIT Drop Pods and Dreadclaws in Horus' army use the reduced costs specified by the Sons of Horus army list. Once per battle, Horus may call down a Lance Strike in his Shooting phase: Weapon Range Str AP Type Lance Strike Unlimited 10 1 Ordnance 1, Blast Resolve this using the normal rules for an Orbital Strike. VESSEL OF THE FOUR Horus counts as a Daemon for all rules, weapons and abilities which specifically affect Daemons. Horus is considered to bear the favour of all four Chaos Gods, but receives no additional characteristic bonuses from Blessings of the Four; these bonuses are already incorporated into his profile. FAVOURED OF THE DARK GODS Whenever an enemy psychic power directly targets or affects Horus, roll a D6 after the Psychic Test is passed. On a 3+, the power is nullified and has no effect upon him. A power which instead directly targets or affects a friendly unit within 6" of Horus is nullified on a 4+. BLESSINGS OF THE FOUR If Horus Ascended is included in the army, Traitor Legiones Astartes Infantry units and Independent Characters may purchase one Blessing of Chaos. A unit may possess only one Blessing, and every model in the unit must purchase the same Blessing. Primarchs may not purchase Blessings. Blessing Unit Cost Independent Character Effect Khorne +5 pts/model +20 pts +1 Attack Slaanesh +4 pts/model +15 pts +1 Initiative Nurgle +7 pts/model +25 pts +1 Toughness and Slow and Purposeful Tzeentch +8 pts/model +25 pts Gain a 5++ save, or improve an existing Invulnerable Save by 1, to a maximum of 4++ The Blessing of Nurgle may not be purchased by Bikes, Jetbikes or Jump Infantry. THE WARMASTER MUST LEAD Horus Ascended may never voluntarily begin the battle in Reserve and must be deployed at the start of the battle whenever the mission permits. If a mission requires Horus to begin in Reserve, he automatically arrives on the first turn.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
