      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Erebus" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-7-high-chaplain-erebus-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvii-7-high-chaplain-erebus-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Erebus | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
MASTER-CRAFTED ACCURSED CROZIUS Erebus' Accursed Crozius follows the normal rules from the Word Bearers Armoury and is additionally Master-crafted. ANATHAME DAGGER During an Assault phase, Erebus may exchange one of his normal Attacks for one attack with the Anathame Dagger. Invulnerable Saves may not be taken against this attack. If the attack inflicts an unsaved Wound upon a non-Vehicle model, it inflicts a Massive Wound (D3) instead of one Wound. Against Vehicles, it has no additional effect. HIGH CHAPLAIN Erebus counts as both a Legion Chaplain Consul and a Diabolist for all Word Bearers rules, army construction requirements and Rites of War. His presence therefore fulfils The Dark Shepherds and allows eligible units to purchase Dark Channelling. BURNING LORE Erebus has Burning Lore at no additional points cost and follows the normal rules presented in the Word Bearers Armoury. COMMAND RETINUE Erebus may select one Legion Command Squad as his retinue. The selected squad does not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot.
Force Organisation:
• HQ
Allegiance:
• Traitor only
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Master-crafted Accursed Crozius
• Bolt pistol
• Anathame Dagger
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Psyker (Mastery Level 1\)
• High Chaplain
• Burning Lore
OPTIONS
• Erebus may take:
• Krak grenades ................................ +2 points
• Melta bombs ................................. +5 points</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-7-high-chaplain-erebus-options" collective="false" import="true">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-7-high-chaplain-erebus-opt-0-krak-grenades">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="r41-unit-xvii-7-high-chaplain-erebus-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" />
