        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xix-2-deliverer-terminator-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Deliverer | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Chieftain | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Deliverers
• 1 Deliverer Chieftain
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• Deliverer Chieftain is a Character
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Combi-bolter
• Power weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard)
• Stubborn
• Terran Veterans
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Deliverers for +43 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Power weapon with:
• Power fist ................................... +10 points
• Chainfist .................................... +15 points
• Pair of Raven's Talons ....................... +10 points
• Any model may replace his Combi-bolter with:
• Combi-flamer ................................. +10 points
• Combi-meltagun ............................... +15 points
• Combi-plasma gun ............................. +15 points
• Combi-volkite charger ........................ +10 points
• One Deliverer for every five models may replace his
Combi-bolter with:
• Heavy flamer ................................. +10 points
• Reaper autocannon ............................ +15 points
• Multi-melta .................................. +20 points
• The Deliverer Chieftain may select up to 50 points of permitted Terminator weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.
TERRAN VETERANS Deliverers are deliberately employed where subtlety has failed. They do not benefit from the Infiltrate ability if it is granted by another Raven Guard rule or Rite of War. They may, however, always deploy using Teleportation Transponders if these have been purchased normally.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
