      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="r41-unit-xix-9-xix-corvus-corax-the-raven-lord-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Corvus Corax" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-9-xix-corvus-corax-the-raven-lord-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xix-9-xix-corvus-corax-the-raven-lord-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Primarch of the Raven Guard, the Raven-Lord, the Deliverer
Corvus Corax was the liberator of Deliverance and master of the XIX Legion, a warrior whose understanding of stealth, infiltration and sudden violence stood apart even among the Primarchs. Raised among the enslaved population of Lycaeus, Corax learned that a stronger enemy need not be met upon ground of its choosing. Instead, its commanders could be isolated, its communications severed and its strength rendered meaningless before the decisive blow was struck.
In battle the Raven-Lord seemed less a general than an apparition, descending upon vital positions before disappearing again into smoke and darkness. His Legion reflected this philosophy, favouring reconnaissance, sabotage and precisely delivered assaults over wars of attrition. The older Raven Guard material likewise centres Corax and his Legion on covert operations, infiltration and lightning strikes rather than headlong assault.
Corvus Corax | 8 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 8 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Corvus Corax
Unit Type:
• Jump Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Sable Armour
• Korvidine Pinions
• Corvidine Talons
• Wrath &amp; Justice
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard)
• The Shadowed Lord
• Surgical Strike
• Sire of the Raven Guard
• Secret Deployment
RESTRICTIONS
Corvus Corax may only be selected for a Loyalist Raven Guard army. He otherwise follows all normal rules and restrictions for Primarchs.
SABLE ARMOUR The black war-plate of the Raven-Lord incorporated sophisticated systems of concealment and disruption, allowing Corax to move through the battlefield with an uncanny ability to escape detection. The Sable Armour counts as Primarch Armour. KORVIDINE PINIONS A highly advanced flight system incorporated into Corax’s armour, the Korvidine Pinions allowed the Raven-Lord to cross the battlefield with a speed and freedom of movement few warriors could match. Corvus Corax is treated as Jump Infantry and follows all normal ProHammer rules for Jump Infantry. His ability to move as Jump Infantry may never be lost, disabled or destroyed as the result of damage to wargear. CORVIDINE TALONS The Corvidine Talons were a matched pair of vicious powered blades designed for the Raven-Lord’s preferred method of sudden and overwhelming close assault. The Corvidine Talons are a matched pair of Power Weapons. Attacks made with them are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Shred and Rending special rules. They count as two close combat weapons. WRATH &amp; JUSTICE Wrath and Justice were a matched pair of archaeotech pistols carried by Corax, their destructive power complementing the speed with which the Raven-Lord closed upon his prey. Weapon Range S AP Type Wrath &amp; Justice 12" 6 4 Assault 2, Rending, Master-crafted THE SHADOWED LORD Corax possessed an almost preternatural ability to disappear amidst darkness, smoke and the confusion of battle, striking without warning before escaping retaliation. Corvus Corax has the Stealth and Hit &amp; Run special rules. SIRE OF THE RAVEN GUARD Under the direction of their gene-sire, the warriors of the XIX Legion exploited every shadow, ruin and fragment of cover to its fullest advantage. Friendly Raven Guard Infantry units with at least one model within 12" of Corvus Corax improve any Cover Save they receive by 1, to a maximum of 3+. SECRET DEPLOYMENT Few enemies ever knew precisely where Corax would strike until the Raven-Lord was already amongst them. Instead of deploying Corvus Corax normally, the Raven Guard player may secretly record one terrain feature which lies outside the enemy deployment zone. Corax is then held off the battlefield.At the beginning of any Raven Guard Movement phase from the second turn onwards, the controlling player may reveal the recorded terrain feature. Place Corax wholly within or in contact with that terrain feature and more than 6" from every enemy model. Corax may Move, Shoot and declare charges normally during the turn in which he is revealed. No Reserve roll is required. If it is impossible to place Corax legally within or in contact with the nominated terrain feature, he may not be revealed that turn and may attempt to deploy there during a later Raven Guard turn. If Corax has selected a Primarch Retinue, the Retinue is deployed normally and does not accompany him when using Secret Deployment. PRIMARCH RETINUE Corvus Corax may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Dark Fury Assault Squad • Raptor Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. Corax may join a Raptor Squad despite the normal restrictions of the Unstable Creation special rule. THE AVENGING SHADOW — POST-ISTVAAN VARIANT Corvus Corax may be fielded as the Avenging Shadow at no additional points cost. This represents Corax during the aftermath of the Dropsite Massacre, clad in hastily repaired armour and consumed by a bitter campaign of vengeance against the Traitor Legions. If this variant is selected, make the following changes: PATCHWORK PANOPLY The shattered armour of the Raven-Lord was repaired with whatever materials could be salvaged in the aftermath of Istvaan, sacrificing some of its former protection for survival and mobility. Corax has a 2+ Armour Save and 4+ Invulnerable Save instead of the normal protection provided by Primarch Armour. His armour still counts as Primarch Armour for all other purposes. GHOST OF ISTVAAN Hunted across the shattered wastes of Istvaan V, Corax became a spectre amongst the ruins, appearing only long enough to kill before vanishing once more. Corax replaces the Stealth special rule granted by The Shadowed Lord with Shrouded. He retains Hit &amp; Run normally. HATER OF TRAITORS The betrayal at Istvaan transformed Corax’s hatred of oppression into a personal and implacable desire for vengeance. Corax has Hatred (Traitor Legiones Astartes).</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="LEGION OPERATIVES" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-0-legion-operatives">
