    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XX — ALPHARIUS, THE HYDRA" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra">
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="490" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" primary="true" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Alpharius" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">7</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Primarch of the Alpha Legion, the Last Primarch, Lord of the XX Legion
Of all the Emperor’s sons, none was surrounded by as much uncertainty as Alpharius. Even within the Alpha Legion, identity was a weapon to be concealed, exchanged and discarded as readily as any blade. Warriors adopted their Primarch’s name and appearance, false commanders led genuine assaults, and seemingly insignificant operations concealed objectives whose importance became apparent only after victory had already been achieved.
Upon the battlefield Alpharius rarely presented the enemy with a single obvious centre of command. His plans were layered with feints, infiltrators and hidden contingencies, allowing the Primarch himself to remain unseen until the precise instant his presence would prove decisive. By the time the enemy understood which warrior truly bore the Pale Spear, the Hydra’s coils had usually closed around them.
Alpharius | 7 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 5 | 6 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Alpharius
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Pythian Scales
• Pale Spear
• Hydra’s Spite
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Master of Lies
• The Hydra
• Sire of the Alpha Legion
• I Am Alpharius
PYTHIAN SCALES The armour of Alpharius incorporated technologies whose origins and capabilities were known only to the inner circles of the XX Legion, its shifting surface and serpentine ornamentation concealing a defence worthy of a Primarch. The Pythian Scales count as Primarch Armour. PALE SPEAR The true origins of the Pale Spear were unknown, though the weapon was believed to be of Xenos manufacture and possessed destructive properties unlike those of the conventional weapons of the Imperium. The Pale Spear is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with the Pale Spear are resolved at Alpharius’ normal Strength and have the Armourbane special rule. Any unsaved Wound inflicted by the Pale Spear against a model without the Primarch special rule becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of one Wound. HYDRA’S SPITE Hydra’s Spite was an ancient plasma weapon of exceptional manufacture, its compact form concealing firepower sufficient to destroy even heavily armoured warriors. Weapon Range S AP Type Hydra’s Spite 18" 7 2 Assault 2, Gets Hot MASTER OF LIES Few commanders could distinguish the true deployment of the XX Legion from the feints and false dispositions which surrounded it. After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, nominate one friendly Alpha Legion unit. That unit may be redeployed anywhere it could legally have been deployed at the beginning of the battle. It must obey all normal deployment restrictions and may not be placed into Reserve unless it was already eligible to begin the battle in Reserve. THE HYDRA Every operation of the Alpha Legion concealed objectives within objectives, the destruction of a seemingly insignificant target often revealing itself as the purpose around which the entire battle had been constructed. Before either army deploys, secretly record one enemy unit as the Alpha Legion’s Priority Target. The identity of the Priority Target need not be revealed until the first time a friendly Alpha Legion unit makes an attack against it. Once revealed, friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when attacking the Priority Target. This applies to both shooting and close combat attacks. SIRE OF THE ALPHA LEGION The warriors of the XX Legion operated according to plans whose true scope was often known only to their Primarch, but the appearance of Alpharius upon the battlefield signalled that those plans had reached their decisive stage. Friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule with at least one model within 12" of Alpharius may use his Leadership characteristic when taking Morale or Pinning tests. I AM ALPHARIUS The Alpha Legion cultivated deliberate uncertainty concerning the appearance and identity of its Primarch. Any warrior might be Alpharius, and an enemy could never be certain that the commander before them was truly the master of the XX Legion until it was already too late. Alpharius is not deployed normally and does not begin the battle in Reserve. At the beginning of any Alpha Legion turn, nominate one friendly Infantry model on the battlefield with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule. Remove that model from play and replace it with Alpharius, placing Alpharius as close as possible to the model’s previous position. The replaced model counts as a casualty. Alpharius enters play with his full starting Wounds and all of his normal wargear and special rules. He does not retain any weapons, wargear, Wounds or other rules possessed by the model he replaced. If the replaced model was part of a unit, Alpharius immediately joins that unit. If the replaced model was engaged in close combat, Alpharius is considered engaged in the same close combat. Alpharius may Move, Shoot and declare charges normally during the turn in which he is revealed. No Reserve roll is required. If Alpharius has not been revealed when the battle ends, he counts as having been slain for the purposes of Victory Points, Slay the Warlord and Price of Failure. PRIMARCH RETINUE Alpharius may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Lernaean Terminator Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. Because Alpharius does not begin the battle on the battlefield, his Primarch Retinue deploys normally without him. Alpharius may use I Am Alpharius to replace a model in his Primarch Retinue. If he does so, he immediately joins that unit. A Lernaean Terminator Squad selected as Alpharius’ Primarch Retinue does not count against the normal 0–1 limitation on Lernaean Terminator Squads.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="KAKOPHONI SQUAD" hidden="true" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad">
