      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r42-role-vii-2-effects-templar-host-templar-brethren-squads-r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Templar Brethren | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+/6+
Templar Champion | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+/6+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
RIGHTEOUS ZEAL Whenever the squad would normally take a Morale test for suffering 25% or more casualties from enemy shooting, it may instead move D6" directly towards the nearest visible enemy unit. This movement may not bring any model within 1" of an enemy model and does not count as charging or Falling Back. If no enemy unit is visible, take the Morale test normally.
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Templar Brethren
• 1 Templar Champion
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Templar Champion is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Combat Shield
• Bolt pistol
• Rending Weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists)
• Stubborn
• Righteous Zeal
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Templar Brethren for +27 points per model.
• Up to five models may replace their Rending Weapon with:
• Power weapon ..................................... +10 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Frag grenades ............................... +1 point per model
• Krak grenades .............................. +2 points per model
• One model may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ................................... +10 points
• One other model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ...................................... +10 points
TEMPLAR CHAMPION
The Templar Champion may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r42-role-vii-2-effects-templar-host-templar-brethren-squads-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false">
          <description>The Templar brethren represent the martial traditions of the VII Legion at their most aggressive.
Where other Imperial Fists formations hold the line or break fortifications through methodical siegecraft, a Templar assault is a direct application of overwhelming force intended to destroy the enemy in close combat.
EFFECTS
TEMPLAR HOST
Templar Brethren Squads may be selected as Troops choices.
They may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
CRUSADING ASSAULT
During an Assault phase in which a Templar Brethren Squad charged after disembarking from a vehicle with the Assault Vehicle special rule during the same player turn, the squad gains the Furious Charge special rule. In addition, its normal charge distance is increased from 6" to 7" for that Assault phase.
SWORDS OF THE LEGION
During the first round of a close combat in which a Templar Brethren Squad charged, models in that squad may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 with:
• Rending Weapons
• Power Weapons
• Relic Blades
• other weapons specifically stated to count as swords
ASSAULT TRANSPORTS
A Templar Brethren Squad may select one of the following as a Dedicated Transport at its normal points cost:
• Land Raider Phobos
• Land Raider Proteus
A Templar Brethren Squad of a size which cannot be carried by either vehicle may instead select a Legion Spartan Assault Tank at its normal points cost.
All normal Transport Capacity restrictions apply.
LIMITATIONS
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Templar Brethren Squads.
The army may include no more than one Fast Attack choice.
The army may not include a Fortification.
The army's Warlord must be equipped with a Power Weapon, Rending Weapon, Relic Blade or another sword-like close-combat weapon which ignores Armour Saves.</description>
        </rule>
