      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r42-role-xvi-1-effects-reaver-onslaught-reaver-attack-squads-r41-unit-xvi-1-reaver-attack-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Reaver | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+
Reaver Chieftain | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Fast Attack
Unit Composition:
• 4 Reavers
• 1 Reaver Chieftain
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Reaver Chieftain is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolt pistol
• Chainaxe
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Furious Charge
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Reavers for +22 points per model.
• Up to two Reavers may replace their Bolt pistol with:
• Flamer .......................................... +5 points
• Meltagun ....................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun ..................................... +15 points
• Plasma Pistol .................................. +15 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Reaver may:
• Replace his Chainaxe with a Power fist ......... +15 points
• Replace his Bolt pistol and Chainaxe with
a pair of Lightning Claws ....................... +15 points
• Every model other than the Reaver Chieftain may purchase:
• Terminator Honours ............................. +15 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
JUMP ASSAULT
The entire squad may purchase Jump Packs for +15 points per model.
If equipped with Jump Packs:
• the unit becomes Jump Infantry;
• it follows the normal ProHammer Jump Infantry rules;
• it may not select a Dedicated Transport.
REAVER CHIEFTAIN
The Reaver Chieftain may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Sons of Horus Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A squad without Jump Packs may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r42-role-xvi-1-effects-reaver-onslaught-reaver-attack-squads-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false">
          <description>The Black Reaving embodies the Cthonian heritage of the XVI Legion. Rather than engaging the enemy in a single ordered battle line, Reaver companies and supporting formations encircle their prey, isolate individual formations and fall upon them from several directions like the gangs of ancient Cthonia.
EFFECTS
REAVER ONSLAUGHT
Reaver Attack Squads may be selected as Troops choices and may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
At least one of the Detachment's compulsory Troops choices must be a Reaver Attack Squad.
CTHONIAN ENCIRCLEMENT
After both armies have been selected, nominate up to two Sons of Horus Infantry units. These units gain the Outflank special rule.
Any Dedicated Transport purchased for one of these units also gains Outflank and enters play together with its passengers.
An Independent Character which begins the battle attached to one of these nominated units may Outflank with it.
When one of the two nominated units enters play, the Sons of Horus player may choose the side table edge from which that unit enters instead of rolling to determine the edge. The other nominated unit follows the normal ProHammer Outflank rules.
LODGE CEREMONY
Once per battle, at the beginning of a Sons of Horus player turn, the Warlord may declare a Lodge Ceremony.
Until the end of that player turn, all non-Vehicle Sons of Horus units gain the Fleet special rule.
CUT THEM APART
During the first round of a close combat, a Sons of Horus unit which charged an enemy unit that was already engaged with another friendly Sons of Horus unit may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1.
This benefit applies only during the player turn in which the unit charged.
LIMITATIONS
The Detachment must include a Legion Centurion upgraded to a Master of Signals Consul.
At least one compulsory Troops choice must be a Reaver Attack Squad.
The Detachment must include at least as many Fast Attack choices as Heavy Support choices.
The Detachment may not include a Fortification or an Allied Detachment.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r42-role-xvi-1-effects-reaver-onslaught-reaver-attack-squads-clone-cleanup" name="Builder compatibility" hidden="false">
          <description>Removed 1 obsolete armoury link(s) inherited from the generic source entry while creating this Rite-specific battlefield-role copy.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
