      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-5-r41-unit-iv-1-iron-havoc-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Iron Havoc | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 3+
Iron Havoc Sergeant | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Heavy Support
Unit Composition:
• 4 Iron Havocs
• 1 Iron Havoc Sergeant
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Iron Havoc Sergeant is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Bolt pistol
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors)
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Iron Havocs
for +25 points per model.
HEAVY WEAPONS
• Up to four Iron Havocs may replace their Bolter with:
• Heavy bolter .................................... +10 points
• Missile Launcher ................................ +15 points
• Autocannon ...................................... +20 points
• Lascannon ....................................... +30 points
SQUAD EQUIPMENT
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ................................... +2 points per model
• Tank Hunters .................................... +3 points per model
IRON HAVOC SERGEANT
• The Iron Havoc Sergeant may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
• The Iron Havoc Sergeant may take:
• Signum .......................................... +15 points
ENHANCED TARGETING Iron Havocs have Ballistic Skill 5, as shown in their profile.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-5-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
