      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-6-r41-unit-iv-2-dominator-cohort-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Dominator | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Dominator Warden | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 3 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Dominators
• 1 Dominator Warden
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Dominator Warden is a Character
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Combi-bolter
• Thunder Hammer
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors)
• Stubborn
• Hatred (Battle-Automata)
• Those Once Honoured
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Dominators
for +50 points per model.
• Any model may replace its Thunder Hammer with:
• Chainfist ........................................ Free
• Any model may replace its Combi-bolter with:
• Volkite charger ................................ +10 points
• Combi-flamer ................................... +10 points
• Combi-meltagun ................................. +15 points
• Combi-plasma gun ............................... +15 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Dominator may replace
its Combi-bolter with:
• Heavy flamer ................................... +10 points
• Reaper autocannon .............................. +15 points
• Multi-Melta .................................... +15 points
• The Dominator Warden may take:
• Grenade Harness ................................ +10 points
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.
HATRED (BATTLE-AUTOMATA) The Dominator Cohort uses the normal ProHammer Hatred special rule when fighting enemy Battle-Automata. THOSE ONCE HONOURED One Dominator Cohort may be selected as Perturabo's personal retinue. If selected in this manner, the squad does not occupy an Elites choice and Perturabo and the Dominator Cohort count as a single HQ selection.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-6-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
