      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-10-r41-unit-vi-1-grey-stalker-pack-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Grey Stalker | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 3+
Stalker Huscarl | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Troops
Unit Composition:
• 4 Grey Stalkers
• 1 Stalker Huscarl
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Stalker Huscarl is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Close-combat weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Night Vision
OPTIONS
• The pack may include up to ten additional Grey Stalkers
for +17 points per model.
• For every five models in the pack, one Grey Stalker may replace his Bolter with:
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Meltagun ...................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun .................................... +15 points
• Volkite Charger ............................... +10 points
• One model may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ............................... +10 points
• One other model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ................................... +10 points
• The entire pack may take:
• Frag grenades ............................ +1 point per model
• Krak grenades ........................... +2 points per model
STALKER HUSCARL
The Stalker Huscarl may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Space Wolves Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A pack of ten models or fewer may select a Rhino, Drop Pod or Dreadclaw Drop Pod. A Grey Stalker Pack embarked upon a Transport may only use Infiltrate if that Transport is itself permitted to deploy using Infiltrate</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-10-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
