          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Wolf Scout Huscarl" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r46-al-reward-11-r41-unit-vi-2-wolf-scout-squad-profile-1">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-11-r41-unit-vi-2-wolf-scout-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Wolf Scout | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 4+
Wolf Scout Huscarl | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 4+
Force Organisation:
BEHIND ENEMY LINES Instead of deploying normally, the Wolf Scout Squad may begin the battle in Reserve, even in a mission which does not normally permit Reserves. When the squad becomes available, nominate any table edge and roll a D6. On a roll of 1, the opposing player chooses the table edge from which the Wolf Scouts enter. On a roll of 2–6, the Space Wolves player chooses the table edge. The squad enters play from the chosen edge using the normal rules for units arriving from Reserve. A Wolf Scout Squad entering play using Behind Enemy Lines may shoot normally, but may not charge during the same turn.
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Wolf Scouts
• 1 Wolf Scout Huscarl
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Wolf Scout Huscarl is a Character
Wargear:
• Scout Armour
• Bolt pistol
• Close-combat weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Behind Enemy Lines
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Wolf Scouts for +14 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Bolt pistol and Close-combat weapon with:
• Bolter ............................................ Free
• Astartes Shotgun .................................. Free
• Sniper Rifle .................................. +5 points
• Up to two Wolf Scouts may each select one of the following:
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Meltagun ...................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun .................................... +15 points
• Plasma pistol ................................. +15 points
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• One Wolf Scout may instead take:
• Heavy Bolter .................................. +10 points
• Missile Launcher ............................. +15 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Frag grenades ............................ +1 point per model
• Krak grenades ........................... +2 points per model
• Melta bombs ............................. +5 points per model
WOLF SCOUT HUSCARL
The Wolf Scout Huscarl may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Space Wolves Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A Wolf Scout Squad may select a Rhino.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-11-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
