      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-16-r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Templar Brethren | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+/6+
Templar Champion | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+/6+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
RIGHTEOUS ZEAL Whenever the squad would normally take a Morale test for suffering 25% or more casualties from enemy shooting, it may instead move D6" directly towards the nearest visible enemy unit. This movement may not bring any model within 1" of an enemy model and does not count as charging or Falling Back. If no enemy unit is visible, take the Morale test normally.
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Templar Brethren
• 1 Templar Champion
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Templar Champion is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Combat Shield
• Bolt pistol
• Rending Weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists)
• Stubborn
• Righteous Zeal
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Templar Brethren for +27 points per model.
• Up to five models may replace their Rending Weapon with:
• Power weapon ..................................... +10 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Frag grenades ............................... +1 point per model
• Krak grenades .............................. +2 points per model
• One model may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ................................... +10 points
• One other model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ...................................... +10 points
TEMPLAR CHAMPION
The Templar Champion may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
