      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-17-r41-unit-vii-1-phalanx-warder-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Phalanx Warder | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+/5+
Warder Sergeant | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+/5+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Phalanx Warders
• 1 Warder Sergeant
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Warder Sergeant is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Boarding Shield
• Bolter
• Power weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists)
• Stubborn
• Counter-Attack
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Phalanx Warders for +28 points per model.
• For every five models, one Phalanx Warder may replace his
Bolter with:
• Flamer ............................................ +5 points
• Meltagun ......................................... +10 points
• Plasma gun ....................................... +15 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Frag grenades ............................... +1 point per model
• Krak grenades .............................. +2 points per model
• Melta bombs ................................ +5 points per model
• One model may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ................................... +10 points
• One other model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ...................................... +10 points
WARDER SERGEANT
The Warder Sergeant may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-17-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
