      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-18-r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Terror Marine | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Headsman | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Terror Marines
• 1 Headsman
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Headsman is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Bolt pistol
• Chainsword
• Frag grenades
• Trophies of Judgement
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)
• Infiltrate
• Preferred Enemy (Infantry)
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Terror Marines
for +25 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Chainsword with:
• Rending Weapon ................................ +5 points
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Any model may replace his Bolter with:
• Volkite Charger .............................. +10 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Terror Marine may
replace his Bolter with:
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Rotor Cannon ................................. +10 points
• Heavy Flamer ................................. +10 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
• Stealth Adept ............................ +1 point per model
HEADSMAN
The Headsman may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Night Lords
Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-18-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
