      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-20-r41-unit-viii-2-contekar-terminator-elite-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Contekar | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/5+
Contekar Dissident | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 2+/5+
NOSTRAMAN CHAINBLADE A Nostraman Chainblade is a Two-Handed Rending Weapon which grants +1 Strength. ESCATON POWER CLAW An Escaton Power Claw counts as a Power Fist. In addition, the wielder may re-roll failed To Wound rolls made with the Escaton Power Claw.
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Contekar
• 1 Contekar Dissident
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Contekar Dissident is a Character
Wargear:
• Tartaros Terminator Armour
• Heavy Flamer
• Nostraman Chainblade
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)
• Stubborn
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Contekar for +50 points per model.
• Every model may replace their Heavy Flamer with:
• Volkite Culverin ........................... +10 points
• Up to two models may replace their Nostraman Chainblade with:
• Escaton Power Claw ........................... +10 points
• The Contekar Dissident may take:
• Grenade Harness .............................. +10 points
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or
Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-20-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
