          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grav Chariot" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r46-al-reward-24-r41-unit-ix-4-grav-chariot-squadron-profile-0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-24-r41-unit-ix-4-grav-chariot-squadron-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Grav Chariot | 4 | 4 | 4 | 5 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 8 | 2+
Force Organisation:
GRAV ENGINES Grav Chariots follow all normal ProHammer rules for Jetbikes. A Grav Chariot may fire both its Twin-linked Bolters and its mounted Heavy Bolter, Multi-Melta or Assault Cannon during the same Shooting phase. The mounted weapon may be fired after the Grav Chariot moves.
• Fast Attack
Unit Composition:
• 1–3 Grav Chariots
Unit Type:
• Jetbike
Wargear:
• Twin-linked Bolters
• Heavy Bolter
• Bolt pistol
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Blood Angels)
• Grav Engines
OPTIONS
• Any Grav Chariot may replace its Heavy Bolter with:
• Multi-Melta ......................................... +15 points
• Assault Cannon ...................................... +20 points</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-24-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
