      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-43-r41-unit-xv-2-ammitara-occult-intercession-cabal-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Ammitara Intercessor | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 4+
Ammitara Fate | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 4+
Force Organisation:
• Fast Attack
PSYCHIC BROTHERHOOD When the army is selected, assign the Cabal to one Prosperine Cult. The Cabal receives both the Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery benefits of that Cult. The Cabal selects one psychic power from: • Divination • Telepathy The Cabal follows all normal ProHammer rules for a Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 1).
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Ammitara Intercessors
• 1 Ammitara Fate
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Ammitara Fate is a Character
Wargear:
• Recon Armour
• Sniper Rifle
• Bolt pistol
• Combat Blade
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)
• Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 1\)
• Scout
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Stealth
OPTIONS
• The Cabal may include up to five additional Ammitara Intercessors for +20 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Sniper Rifle with:
• Combi-flamer ................................. +10 points
• Combi-volkite charger ....................... +10 points
• Combi-meltagun .............................. +15 points
• Combi-plasma gun ............................ +15 points
• Up to two models may instead replace their Sniper Rifle with:
• Meltagun ..................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun ................................... +15 points
• One model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ................................... +10 points
• The entire Cabal may take:
• Krak grenades .......................... +2 points per model
• Melta bombs ............................ +5 points per model
AMMITARA FATE
The Ammitara Fate may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-43-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
