      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-50-r41-unit-xvii-1-gal-vorbak-dark-brethren-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Dark Brethren | 5 | 4 | 5 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 2 | 9 | 3+/5+
Dark Martyr | 5 | 4 | 5 | 5 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 3+/5+
RENDING The Rending special rule applies only to the Gal Vorbak's close-combat attacks.
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Allegiance:
• Traitor only
Unit Composition:
• 4 Dark Brethren
• 1 Dark Martyr
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Dark Martyr is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Bolt pistol
• Close-combat weapon
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)
• Daemon
• Fearless
• Bulky
• Rending
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Dark Brethren for +30 points per model.
• For every five models in the squad, one Dark Brethren may replace his Bolter with:
• Flamer ........................................ +5 points
• Meltagun ..................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun ................................... +15 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Dark Brethren may
replace his Close-combat weapon with:
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Power fist .................................... +15 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
DARK MARTYR
The Dark Martyr may replace his Close-combat weapon with:
• Power weapon ................................... +10 points
• Power fist ...................................... +15 points
• Lightning claw ................................. +15 points
The Dark Martyr may take:
• Artificer Armour ............................... +10 points
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.
When using Last of the Serrated Sun, the squad follows the additional transport requirements of that Rite of War.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-50-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
