      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r46-al-reward-54-r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-source" hidden="false">
          <description>Pyroclast | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 2+
Pyroclast Warden | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 10 | 2+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Pyroclasts
• 1 Pyroclast Warden
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Pyroclast Warden is a Character
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Pyroclast Flame Projector
• Bolt pistol
• Close-combat weapon
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Salamanders)
• Stubborn
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Pyroclasts for +30 points per model.
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
PYROCLAST WARDEN
The Pyroclast Warden may replace his Close-combat weapon with:
• Rending Weapon ................................ +5 points
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Power fist .................................... +15 points
• Thunder hammer ............................... +20 points
The Pyroclast Warden may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Salamanders Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.
PYROCLAST FLAME PROJECTOR Each time a Pyroclast Flame Projector is fired, choose one of the following: • It may fire as a Salamanders Heavy Flamer. • It may fire as a Meltagun. The selected weapon uses all of its normal rules. For the purposes of Promethean Cult and Fire-based Warfare, the weapon counts as the weapon whose profile it is using.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="r46-al-reward-54-rule" name="The Rewards of Treachery" hidden="false">
          <description>One eligible Legion-specific unit from another Legion may be selected as an Elites choice. It retains its profile, equipment, options and unit-specific special rules, but replaces its original Legion-specific Legiones Astartes rules with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) and benefits from Alpha Legion rules including Mutable Tactics.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
